s mass production possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/07/31/world/canada/leone-farrell-chemist.html', 'snippet': 'An American researcher created the polio vaccine, but a Toronto lab and a pioneering female scientist made its mass production possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Canadians don’t have to go back to 1918 and the start of the Spanish flu pandemic to find an analogy to today. For decades, waves of polio outbreaks gripped the country with fear, death and uncertainty, as recently as the 1950s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/31/world/31canadaletter/31canadaletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/07/31/world/31canadaletter/31canadaletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 469}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/31/world/31canadaletter/31canadaletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/31/world/31canadaletter/31canadaletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/31/world/31canadaletter/31canadaletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/07/31/world/31canadaletter/31canadaletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/07/31/world/31canadaletter/31canadaletter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada’s Key Role in Creating a Once Awaited Vaccine', 'kicker': 'CANADA LeTTER', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-01T01:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Canada', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33db8345-99a1-54a4-bc52-e9a544cdcf89', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33db8345-99a1-54a4-bc52-e9a544cdcf89'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, August 1, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/07/31/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-china-wields-its-security-law-to-crush-hong-kong-dissent.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, August 1, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '“They are running short of confidence to face the people, to face the people’s choice, to face the people’s demands. It’s fear.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: China Wields Its Security Law to Crush Hong Kong Dissent', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-01T03:42:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://ar