s since 1996, although it’s been a bit since we’ve seen one of his Sundays. He’s been busy: He was a head writer for the recent television iterations of the “$100,000 Pyramid” and “Cash Cab,” and he wrote for “Who Wants to be a Millionaire” for nine years. Those impressive trivia chops come into play today in the fill, and the theme is good wordplay.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/crosswords/02wordplay-delft/02wordplay-delft-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/02/crosswords/02wordplay-delft/02wordplay-delft-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/crosswords/02wordplay-delft/02wordplay-delft-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/crosswords/02wordplay-delft/02wordplay-delft-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1317, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/crosswords/02wordplay-delft/02wordplay-delft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/02/crosswords/02wordplay-delft/02wordplay-delft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/crosswords/02wordplay-delft/02wordplay-delft-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Puzzlin’', 'kicker': 'Wordplay, the CROSSWORD COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilk, David Levinson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-01T21:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0417cba2-30aa-5da4-8f1e-0b78c763b39a', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0417cba2-30aa-5da4-8f1e-0b78c763b39a'}, {'abstract': 'Her near-total transplant in 2008 was at the time the most complex one ever performed. She was the fourth patient in the world to undergo such a procedure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/01/us/Connie-culp-dead-face-transplant.html', 'snippet': 'Her near-total transplant in 2008 was at the time the most complex one ever performed. She was the fourth patient in the world to undergo such a procedure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Connie Culp, the first patient in the United States to receive a face transplant, died on Wednesday at the Cleveland Clinic, where her procedure was performed in 2008. She was 57.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/04/multimedia/01xp-connieculp-pix1/merlin_175200339_febffdf5-1c8c-47cb-96b2-27c133295c8d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/04/multimedia/01xp-connieculp-pix1/merlin_175200339_febffdf5-1c8c-47cb