tial Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 1960', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-03T09:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4631e1ae-4d14-5dc6-9439-b02b68d50275', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4631e1ae-4d14-5dc6-9439-b02b68d50275'}, {'abstract': 'Resistance to eliminating it has long been connected to the idea of white supremacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/03/opinion/electoral-college-racism-white-supremacy.html', 'snippet': 'Resistance to eliminating it has long been connected to the idea of white supremacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As our revived national conversation on race has made clear, the legacies of slavery and white supremacy run wide and deep in American society and political life. One such legacy — which is particularly noteworthy in a presidential election season — has been the survival and preservation of the Electoral College, an institution that has been under fire for more than 200 years. Our complicated method of electing presidents has been the target of recurrent reform attempts since the early 19th century, and the politics of race and region have figured prominently in their defeat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_p