e', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/opinion/03Lovell1/merlin_175146375_96b5f246-7b90-4ab9-8501-cd53c0c0c636-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/03/opinion/03Lovell1/merlin_175146375_96b5f246-7b90-4ab9-8501-cd53c0c0c636-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/opinion/03Lovell1/merlin_175146375_96b5f246-7b90-4ab9-8501-cd53c0c0c636-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/opinion/03Lovell1/merlin_175146375_96b5f246-7b90-4ab9-8501-cd53c0c0c636-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/opinion/03Lovell1/03Lovell1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/03/opinion/03Lovell1/03Lovell1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/opinion/03Lovell1/03Lovell1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m the Police Chief in Portland. Violence Isn’t the Answer.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Violence  Is Not  An Answer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Reform', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal-State Relations (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-03T19:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Lovell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c27f480-aa31-5d22-827d-264461f680ea', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c27f480-aa31-5d22-827d-264461f680ea'}, {'abstract': 'Ways to create a multiracial and multicultural spectrum in a child’s activities and toys.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/03/parenting/multiracial-toys-diversity-play.html', 'snippet': 'Ways to create a multiracial and multicultural spectrum in a child’s activities and toys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Becoming a mother made me reflect on my own childhood and how I was raised to view diversity. I grew up in South Georgia at a time when dolls of my complexion were not easy to find. So I played with mostly white dolls. The features I observed in Ken and Barbie were exactly what I saw around me: the familiar aspect of white people. My doctor was white. My teachers were mostly white. Police officers and bank tellers all had skin that did not look like my own.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Diversify Your Toy Box', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diversify Your Child’s Toy Box', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-03T19:35:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shanicia Boswell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shanicia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boswell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c895dc8a-4a12-5a56-80db-753f0d01abd7', 'word_count': 1600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c895dc8a-4a12-5a56-80db-753f0d01abd7'}, {'abstract': 'Within a storied Los Angeles studio complex, Karina Deyko and David de Rothschild have built an eclectic, freewheeling space in which to live and work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/03/t-magazine/david-de-rothschild-venice-home-design.html', 'snippet': 'Within a storied Los Angeles studio complex, Karina Deyko and David de Rothschild have built an eclectic, freewheeling space in which to live and work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the British environmentalist David de Rothschild was at sea in the spring of 2010, crossing the Pacific Ocean on the Plastiki —\xa0a 60-foot catamaran built primarily from recycled bottles —\xa0to raise awareness about the climate crisis, the actress Karina Deyko, his wife, made her own voyage of discovery. She had recently met, through a mutual friend in Los Angeles, the actress Kelly Reilly and the photographer Guy Webster, who helped establish the tenets of rock ’n’ roll portraiture in the 1960s with his images of Jim Morrison and the Rolling Stones. Reilly had been renting a small apartment within Webster’s sprawling studio complex in Venice Beach but would soon be traveling to London to make a film. Webster wondered if Deyko wanted to come see the space and possibly sublet it. At the time, she was living in Echo Park, on the east side of the city, and “I knew that when David was done with the Plastiki he’d want to be by the beach,” Deyko says. So she took Webster up on his offer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/t-magazine/design/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/03/t-magazine/design/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/t-magazine/design/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/t-magazine/design/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/t-magazine/design/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/03/t-magazine/design/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX/3tmag-rothschild-slide-2WRX-thumbStandard