ice-centric urban culture despite the pandemic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/nyregion/03nyfacebook-1/03nyfacebook-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/03/nyregion/03nyfacebook-1/03nyfacebook-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/nyregion/03nyfacebook-1/03nyfacebook-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/nyregion/03nyfacebook-1/03nyfacebook-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/nyregion/03nyfacebook-1/03nyfacebook-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/03/nyregion/03nyfacebook-1/03nyfacebook-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/03/nyregion/03nyfacebook-1/03nyfacebook-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Bets Big on Future of N.Y.C., and Offices, With New Lease', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Farley, James A, General Post Office (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-03T21:35:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Haag', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haag', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8421abc8-f280-5fb8-b2e2-ebc6deab0e9b', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8421abc8-f280-5fb8-b2e2-ebc6deab0e9b'}, {'abstract': 'The West Village store also ships nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/03/dining/new-york-biltong.html', 'snippet': 'The West Village store also ships nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Biltong is South African beef jerky, succulent and less stringy than the American kind, and this new West Village food store specializes in it. The house biltong is made from traditional grass-fed or aged beef, among other options, and thin little slices often have a richness that’s worthy of a platter or cheese board. The owners of the shop, Camran St. Luce and Brittney Brothers, also sell meat pies, sausages, chutneys, South African beers and ciders, and other goods. Everything except beer and cider is available nationwide on the website. The shop opens Aug. 4.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/05/dining/03burner-meat/03burner-meat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/05/dining/03burner-meat/03burner-meat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargehei