rson': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9179e28a-1e81-5997-8275-8f11dbd59346', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9179e28a-1e81-5997-8275-8f11dbd59346'}, {'abstract': 'Helados La Neta is High Road Craft’s new line of flavors including coconut, avocado and lime, and rum raisin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/03/dining/mexican-ice-cream.html', 'snippet': 'Helados La Neta is High Road Craft’s new line of flavors including coconut, avocado and lime, and rum raisin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This has been the summer of new ice creams. I suppose that when you’re sheltering in place, there’s nothing more tempting than a pint and a spoon. A line of inviting Mexican-inspired flavors called Helados La Neta has been introduced by High Road Craft, a bakery and ice cream company in Marietta, Ga. (The company also makes Ciao Bella.) Among the offerings are a distinctive vanilla; cinnamon-scented horchata; deep chocolate; nubbly coconut; delicate strawberries and cream; rum raisin; and avocado and lime. The ice creams are sold at Walmart, ShopRite and Kroger stores, among others.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/05/dining/03burner-cream/03burner-cream-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/05/dining/03burner-cream/03burner-cream-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/05/dining/03burner-cream/03burner-cream-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', '