 a Klansman,” by Edward Ball', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/04/books/review/life-of-a-klansman-by-edward-ball-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Life of a Klansman,” by Edward Ball', 'lead_paragraph': 'The middle of the week is good for an attack, for the surprise. It is March 4, 1873, in the city of New Orleans, a Tuesday night. About 9:00 p.m., a man called Polycarp Constant Lecorgne emerges from his house by the levee of the Mississippi River. He is a forty-one-year-old carpenter. Constant Lecorgne and his wife, Gabrielle Duchemin, live in a neighborhood called Bouligny. They have six children, and Gabrielle is pregnant with another. Gabrielle and the children remain in the house when Constant leaves for the night. He carries a gun, probably a revolver. The U.S. Army confiscated most of the long guns years ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Life of a Klansman,’ by Edward Ball: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-04T09:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa539e3-e59d-5751-8729-057635e3d624', 'word_count': 1145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa539e3-e59d-5751-8729-057635e3d624'}, {'abstract': 'Tens of millions of Americans have lost crucial jobless benefits, and lawmakers still can’t seem to agree on a relief measure. Israel’s troubled school reopenings could be a lesson for the U.S.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/04/world/coronavirus-cases.html', 'snippet': 'Tens of millions of Americans have lost crucial jobless benefits, and lawmakers still can’t seem to agree on a relief measure. Israel’s troubled school reopenings could be a lesson for the U.S.', 'lead_paragraph'