zation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4105dbc1-827f-5bf7-bf35-2a05f63b60cc', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4105dbc1-827f-5bf7-bf35-2a05f63b60cc'}, {'abstract': 'Led by the members of the Atlanta Dream, players have begun wearing T-shirts supporting a political opponent of Senator Kelly Loeffler, who co-owns the Dream and has spoken against the Black Lives Matter movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/04/sports/basketball/wnba-dream-loeffler-warnock.html', 'snippet': 'Led by the members of the Atlanta Dream, players have begun wearing T-shirts supporting a political opponent of Senator Kelly Loeffler, who co-owns the Dream and has spoken against the Black Lives Matter movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Players for the Atlanta Dream and other teams across the W.N.B.A. have begun a public show of defiance by wearing T-shirts endorsing the Democratic opponent of the Dream’s co-owner Senator Kelly Loeffler, Republican of Georgia, who is in a tightly contested race for her seat and has spoken disparagingly of the Black Lives Matter movement.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/05/sports/05WNBA-PRINT/05WNBA-PRINT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/05/sports/05WNBA-PRINT/05WNBA-PRINT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 471}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/05/sports/05WNBA-PRINT/05WNBA-PRINT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 804, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/05/sports/05WNBA-PRINT/05WNBA-PRINT-superJumbo.j