eek before, when my husband mentioned that his cousin S., who lives far away, would be visiting the area and wanted to come over for dinner in our Hudson, N.Y., backyard, and I paused.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/opinion/07harmanci-illo/05harmanci-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/07/opinion/07harmanci-illo/05harmanci-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 547}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/opinion/07harmanci-illo/05harmanci-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 934, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/opinion/07harmanci-illo/05harmanci-illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1869, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/opinion/07harmanci-illo/05harmanci-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/07/opinion/07harmanci-illo/05harmanci-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/opinion/07harmanci-illo/05harmanci-illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Backyard Dinner, Coronavirus Chaos Ensues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dinner Guest, Then Viral Chaos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contact Tracing (Public Health)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Risks and Safety Concerns', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-05T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reyhan Harmanci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reyhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harmanci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a1258ef-4878-53cb-901e-e7bd2024c96e', 'word_count': 1467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a1258ef-4878-53cb-901e-e7bd2024c96e'}, {'abstract': 'Physical demands required for work may have negative consequences for brain health, a new study suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/05/well/move/can-a-physically-taxing-job-be-bad-for-our-brains.html', 'snippet': 'Physical demands required for work may have negative consequences for brain health, a new study suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regular exercise helps to bulk up our brains and improve thinking skills, numerous studies show. But physically demanding jobs, even if they are being carried out in an office, might have a different and opposite effect, according to a provocative new study of almost 100 older people and their brains and work histories. It finds that men and women who considered their work to be physically draining tended to have smaller memory centers in their brains and lower scores on memory tests than other people whose jobs felt less physically taxing.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/11/well/physed-store/physed-store-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/11/well/physed-store/physed-store-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/11/well/physed-store/physed-store-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/11/well/physed-store/physed-store-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/11/well/physed-store/physed-store-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/11/well/physed-store/physed-store-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/11/well/physed-store/physed-store-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can a Physically Taxing Job Be Bad for Our Brains?', 'kicker': 'Phys Ed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Working Out, and Just Plain Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-05T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Move', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a49b2a14-690d-5356-b2df-596f8b97ff91', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a49b2a14-690d-5356-b2df-596f8b97ff91'}, {'abstract': 'From a sniffle or cough that feels like allergies to severe body aches and crippling fatigue, the symptoms of coronavirus can be unpredictable from head to toe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/05/well/live/coronavirus-covid-symptoms.html', 'snippet': 'From a sniffle or cough that feels like allergies to severe body aches and crippling fatigue, the symptoms of coronavirus can be unpredictable from head to toe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a Texas nurse, the first sign that something was wrong happened while brushing her teeth — she couldn’t taste her toothpaste. For a Georgia attorney, it was hitting a wall of fatigue on a normally easy run. When a Wisconsin professor fell ill in June, he thought a bad meal had upset his stomach.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/11/science/05WELL-COVIDSYMPTOMS3/merlin_173813931_b87dc1ca-a27d-476a-9528-7b813b9a5438-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/11/science/05WELL-COVIDSYMPTOMS3/merlin_173813931_b87dc1ca-a27d-476a-9528-7b813b9a5438-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i