et': 'A generational comedy starring Seth Rogen makes its debut. And a classic Stephen King story airs on Starz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AN AMERICAN PICKLE (2020) Stream on HBO. In 1919, Herschel Greenbaum (Seth Rogen) and his wife, Sarah (Sarah Snook), emigrated from their fictional Eastern European home country — a place called Schlupsk — to New York City, where they dreamed of building a better life for generations of Greenbaums to come. But one fateful day, Herschel fell into a vat of brine at a pickle factory, where he worked. When Herschel emerged from the pickle vat, perfectly preserved 100 years later, he found there was only one Greenbaum left: his great-grandson, Ben (also Rogen). With Ben, Herschel becomes determined to refine the Greenbaum legacy once more. The film’s screenplay is written by Simon Rich and is adapted from his 2013 novella, “Sell Out.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/06/arts/06tvcol-1/06tvcol-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/06/arts/06tvcol-1/06tvcol-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/06/arts/06tvcol-1/06tvcol-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/06/arts/06tvcol-1/06tvcol-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1236, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/06/arts/06tvcol-1/06tvcol-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType