s', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/arts/06streetart-notebook19/06streetart-notebook19-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/07/arts/06streetart-notebook19/06streetart-notebook19-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/arts/06streetart-notebook19/06streetart-notebook19-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/arts/06streetart-notebook19/06streetart-notebook19-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/arts/06streetart-notebook19/06streetart-notebook19-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/07/arts/06streetart-notebook19/06streetart-notebook19-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/arts/06streetart-notebook19/06streetart-notebook19-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Sidewalk Prophets Are Heirs of the Artisans of France’s Lascaux Caves', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Listen to the Thunder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-06T09:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seph Rodney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rodney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8209a98-e31d-5b9f-9356-48d427152c69', 'word_count': 1429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8209a98-e31d-5b9f-9356-48d427152c69'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Luster,” by Raven Leilani', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/06/books/review/luster-by-raven-leilani-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Luster,” by Raven Leilani', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time we have sex, we are both fully clothed, at our desks during working hours, bathed in blue computer light. He is uptown processing a new bundle of microfiche and I am downtown handling corrections for a new Labrador detective manuscript. He tells me what he ate for lunch and asks if I can manage to take off my underwear in my cubicle without anyone noticing. His messages come with impeccable punctuation. He is fond of words like taste and spread. The empty text field is full of possibilities. Of course I worry about IT remoting into my computer, or my internet history warranting yet another disciplinary meeting with HR. But the risk. The thrill of a third pair of unseen eyes. The idea that someone in the office, with that sweet, post-lunch-break optimism, might come across the thread and see how tenderly Eric and I have built this private world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Luster,’ by Raven Leilani: An Excerpt', 'kicker': No