www.nytimes.com/2020/08/07/opinion/tiktok-wechat-china-trump-executive-order.html', 'snippet': 'His foolish and dangerous edicts suggest that the United States, like China, no longer believes in a global internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The one thing my students all invariably know about China is that you can’t use Facebook there, or YouTube or Google. For at least a decade, China has maintained strict control over the internet and aggressively blocked foreign tech platforms within its borders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/opinion/10Wolff/07Wolff-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/10/opinion/10Wolff/07Wolff-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/opinion/10Wolff/07Wolff-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/opinion/10Wolff/07Wolff-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1327, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/opinion/10Wolff/07Wolff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/10/opinion/10Wolff/07Wolff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/opinion/10Wolff/07Wolff-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So What Does Trump Have Against TikTok?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TikTok (ByteDance)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WeChat (Mobile App)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacklisting', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-07T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josephine Wolff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josephine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcfb1ce5-89f5-5281-81cd-ad5ad44caa79', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcfb1ce5-89f5-5281-81cd-ad5ad44caa79'}, {'abstract': 'The author’s stories have influenced countless works, including the new HBO series “Lovecraft Country.” But how do modern adapters reckon with his racism, his sexism and his profound weirdness?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/07/arts/television/hp-lovecraft.html', 'snippet': 'The author’s stories have influenced countless works, including the new HBO series “Lovecraft Country.” But how do modern adapters reckon with his racism, his sexism and his profound weirdness?', 'lead_paragraph': '“Lovecraft Country,” premiering Aug. 16 on HBO, follows a Black family entangled in eldritch phenomena. Based on Matt Ruff’s 2016 novel, the series is a sideways look at the terrors of Jim Crow America that nods to and reframes the work of H.P. Lovecraft, the widely cited if narrowly read pulp fiction writer from the early 20th century.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/arts/09LOVECRAFT-MAN1/merlin_175074234_2498e472-bcd6-4f63-bd57-5780e8d8e347-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/09/arts/09LOVECRAFT-MAN1/merlin_175074234_2498e472-bcd6-4f63-bd57-5780e8d8e347-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 736}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/arts/09LOVECRAFT-MAN1/merlin_175074234_2498e472-bcd6-4f63-bd57-5780e8d8e347-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 836, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/arts/09LOVECRAFT-MAN1/merlin_175074234_2498e472-bcd6-4f63-bd57-5780e8d8e347-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1751, 'width': 1428, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/arts/09LOVECRAFT-MAN1/09LOVECRAFT-MAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_