pest Divisions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Uribe, Alvaro', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-07T09:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turkewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b286aa3-9ef9-5723-9b69-35b6e65c74c6', 'word_count': 1543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b286aa3-9ef9-5723-9b69-35b6e65c74c6'}, {'abstract': 'But history has a way of confounding those who think they can control it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/07/opinion/trump-2020-census.html', 'snippet': 'But history has a way of confounding those who think they can control it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last few years, the Trump administration has fought to shape the 2020 census to its political benefit and the benefit of the Republican Party. In 2018, it sought to introduce a citizenship question on the census itself, to reduce response rates among immigrant communities. Then, after that was rebuffed by the Supreme Court, it tried to exclude unauthorized immigrants altogether, in direct conflict with the Constitution, which calls on Congress to count “the whole number of persons in each State.” Now it wants to cut the census short and deliver it uncompleted — a last-ditch effort to rig the nation’s politics for the sake of its exclusionary political vision.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/08/opinion/08bouie_print/merlin_153869544_fe018d11-1ded-4eef-909b-30ab36d22516-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/08/opinion/08bouie_print/merlin_153869544_fe018d11-1ded-4eef-909b-30ab36d22516-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/08/opinion/08bouie_print/merlin_153869544_fe018d11-1ded-4eef-909b-30ab36d22516-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/08/opinion/08bouie_print/merlin_153869544_fe018d11-1ded-4eef-909b-30ab36d22516-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/08/opinion/08bouie_print/07bouieWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/08/opinion/08bouie_print/07bouieWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/08/opinion/08bouie_print/07bouieWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump and His Allies Think They Know Who Counts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline