otest, the first time that he had ever gone to a march. Clare Ramirez-Raftree said she ended up with welts on her wrists for days from the tight plastic handcuffs. And Patrick McElravey said police officers put him in a chokehold in Brooklyn.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Were Arrested During the Protests. Here’s What Happened Next.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out of the Crowd, Into the Hands of the Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Bronx (Bronx, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Downtown Brooklyn (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Army Plaza (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-07T09:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ali Watkins and Simbarashe Cha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Watkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Simbarashe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da6513fc-9cbe-5359-8ab7-eb9c05a99915', 'word_count': 1962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da6513fc-9cbe-5359-8ab7-eb9c05a99915'}, {'abstract': 'Tara Harper knew Fritz Rahr was “the one” after he volunteered to join her on a tr