iled up for years that nursing homes were vulnerable. The pandemic sent them to the back of the line for equipment and care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/08/world/europe/coronavirus-nursing-homes-elderly.html', 'snippet': 'Warnings had piled up for years that nursing homes were vulnerable. The pandemic sent them to the back of the line for equipment and care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Shirley Doyen was exhausted. The Christalain nursing home, which she ran with her brother in an affluent neighborhood in Brussels, was buckling from Covid-19. Eight residents had died in three weeks. Some staff members had only gowns and goggles from Halloween doctor costumes for protection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Covid-19 Hit, Many Elderly Were Left to Die', 'kicker': 'Behind the Curve', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Covid Hit,  The World Let  Its Elderly Die', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protective Clothing and Gear', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-08T09:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matina Stevis-Gridneff, Matt Apuzzo, Monika Pronczuk and Mauricio Lima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevis-Gridneff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': '