ganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9fbbb0f-f486-50af-8f68-606651acb1eb', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9fbbb0f-f486-50af-8f68-606651acb1eb'}, {'abstract': 'Co-op boards do not like to get in the middle of resident disputes. But if one shareholder is tormenting another, the issue must be addressed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/08/realestate/neighbor-complaints-co-ops.html', 'snippet': 'Co-op boards do not like to get in the middle of resident disputes. But if one shareholder is tormenting another, the issue must be addressed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q: The rear windows of my apartment in a Westchester co-op overlook a small outdoor sitting area with views of woods, birds, squirrels and chipmunks. Since spring, a new resident as been grilling there, obliterating the serenity of the space. After shareholders complained, the board insisted he move his grill 10 feet from the wall, but didn’t make any other demands. He’s still out there daily with two grills, chairs and an enormous toy car. He shouts and blasts his music. When I complained to management, I was told that he’s allowed to grill. But what about my comfort and my rights to use the space that he now dominates?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/realestate/09ASK/merlin_175292247_1a0dcd70-c345-4ffb-bd90-909125e4079d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 118, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/09/realestate/09ASK/merlin_175292247_1a0dcd70-c345-4ffb-bd90-909125e4079d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 118}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/realestate/09ASK/merlin_175292247_1a0dcd70-c345-4ffb-bd90-909125e4079d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 201, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/realestate/09ASK/merlin_175292247_1a0dcd70-c345-4ffb-bd90-909125e4079d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/realestate/09ASK/09ASK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/09/realestate/09ASK/09ASK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/09/realestate/09ASK/09ASK-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Neighbor vs. Neighbor in a Co-op. Who Wins?', 'kicker': 'Ask Real Estate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Can I Get My Co-op to Intervene In a Dispute With Another Resident?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooperatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-08T14:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronda Kaysen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaysen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d817fb0-a0ca-5ac1-ae9b-f40339ce0b1b', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': '