major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disease Rates', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-08T18:28:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/61e03b0b-c9c3-5673-93e1-6ea0a7ebb414', 'word_count': 1243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61e03b0b-c9c3-5673-93e1-6ea0a7ebb414'}, {'abstract': 'The players, who have pushed for more-frequent virus testing and stronger protection of their status with the team, said Pac-12 Commissioner Larry Scott offered no concrete mandates for the league’s universities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/08/sports/ncaafootball/coronavirus-pac-12-players-larry-scott.html', 'snippet': 'The players, who have pushed for more-frequent virus testing and stronger protection of their status with the team, said Pac-12 Commissioner Larry Scott offered no concrete mandates for the league’s universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a group of Pac-12 Conference players who are threatening to opt out of the football season met with Commissioner Larry Scott on Thursday night, they had two primary objectives: pushing for more-frequent coronavirus testing and protecting the eligibility and status of players who choose not to play for health reasons.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/sports/08pac12-2-print/merlin_165542769_b9f4833d-ffdd-4da2-a8fe-ab80c9da179f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/10/