er decades in captivity and a 1,700-mile road trip from Argentina into Brazil, an Asian elephant named Mara finally gained a chance to roam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/09/science/coronavirus-elephants-wildlife-zoo.html', 'snippet': 'After decades in captivity and a 1,700-mile road trip from Argentina into Brazil, an Asian elephant named Mara finally gained a chance to roam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The border between Argentina and Brazil had been closed by the coronavirus pandemic for nearly two months when, in early May, an unusual convoy approached the checkpoint in Puerto Iguazú. There were 15 people, all of whom had gone days with little sleep, and six vehicles, including a crane and a large truck.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Move Your Elephant During a Pandemic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unforgettable Journey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elephants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildlife Sanctuaries and Nature Reserves', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-photojournalism', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-animals', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-09T09:00:30+0000', 