, 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb471beb-5a22-5ec2-8138-0d6e9f23957a', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb471beb-5a22-5ec2-8138-0d6e9f23957a'}, {'abstract': 'Marina Moscone makes elegant women’s wear that privileges handcraft and meticulous attention to detail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/10/t-magazine/marina-moscone-fashion-design.html', 'snippet': 'Marina Moscone makes elegant women’s wear that privileges handcraft and meticulous attention to detail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the New York-based women’s wear designer Marina Moscone was 3, she stole her father’s burgundy leather briefcase and used it to carry around the sketches she made wherever she went. Not long after, she announced to her parents that she was becoming a fashion designer. A few years later, at age 7, she decided that she would eventually move from her native Vancouver, British Columbia, to New York to study at the Parsons School of Design. She had learned about the school while watching reruns of the Canadian TV show “Fashion File.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/t-magazine/art/Tadobe-slide-PWCG/Tadobe-slide-PWCG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/10/t-magazine/art/Tadobe-slide-PWCG/Tadobe-slide-PWCG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/t-magazine/art/Tadobe-slide-PWCG/Tadobe-slide-PWCG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/