differently: a whey-based ricotta from Caputo Brothers Creamery in Spring Grove, Pa.; whole-milk Renaissance Ricotta from Narragansett Creamery in Providence; Salvatore Ricotta from Brooklyn, N.Y., made with whole milk and heavy cream; and ricotta lana, a sheep’s milk ricotta from Vermont Shepherd in Westminster, Vt. In October, there will be three Alpine-style cheeses, with two samples of each at different ages. Winter brings three runny bark-wrapped examples, and, in spring, there will a set of bloomy rind cheeses to try.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerCheese01/10BurnerCheese01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerCheese01/10BurnerCheese01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerCheese01/10BurnerCheese01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerCheese01/10BurnerCheese01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerCheese01/10BurnerCheese01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerCheese01/10BurnerCheese01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerCheese01/10BurnerCheese01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cheese Club From a Noted Cheesemonger', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sample: A Cheese Club From A Noted Cheesemonger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saxelby Cheesemongers (Manhattan, NY, Retailer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-11T00:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10402e58-ce96-5ffd-bdda-1453c28b92ea', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10402e58-ce96-5ffd-bdda-1453c28b92ea'}, {'abstract': 'Marco Sweets & Spices, a new frozen treat company, hopes to take its clients to other places through its flavors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/10/dining/marco-sweets-and-spices-ice-cream.html', 'snippet': 'Marco Sweets & Spices, a new frozen treat company, hopes to take its clients to other places through its flavors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The right tastes can transport you to places that may not be on your itinerary for now. That’s the idea that inspired the owners of the New York company, Marco Sweets & Spices, to create confections that suggest flavorful destinations. A Thai coco-lime ice cream is fueled by chile powder. Aztec Chocolate is scented with cinnamon and spiked with chile. Vanilla Chai and Ginger Dreamsicle with orange are a couple of others. The seasonings come from Brooklyn Spice Company in Greenpoint, Brooklyn. Luke Christianson, Avery Henderson, Spencer Joynt and Julian Plyter, a veteran of Le Bernardin and a founder of Melt Bakery, make up the team.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerMarco01/10BurnerMarco01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerMarco01/10BurnerMarco01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerMarco01/10BurnerMarco01-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerMarco01/10BurnerMarco01-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1240, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerMarco01/10BurnerMarco01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerMarco01/10BurnerMarco01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/dining/10BurnerMarco01/10BurnerMarco01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'These Ice Creams Are Transporting', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Spoon: These Ice Creams  Are Transporting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Cream and Frozen Desserts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marco Sweets & Spices (Retailer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-11T00:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a697929-ffa0-5686-8507-92f2fe669ce3', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a697929-ffa0-5686-8507-92f2fe669ce3'}, {'abstract': 'These ribs arrive, by way of Lewis Barbecue in Charleston, S.C., ready for a few hours of cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/10/dining/lewis-barbecue-ribs.html', 'snippet': 'These ribs arrive, by way of Lewis Barbecue in Charleston, S.C., ready for a few hours of cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summon your inner caveperson with this rack of Texas-style smoked beef ribs from Lewis Barbecue in Charleston, S.C. Three immense bones come thickly surrounded by succulent spiced and blackened slabs of smoked meat, enough for a Stone Age party of six. Newly available nationwide, they are shipped frozen and deserve a slow defrost overnight before you open the package, rewrap them in foil and bake for a couple of hours. Lewis is also selling pork ribs. Along with the ribs, a bottle of Lewis’s barbecue sauce could go on the table, especially the Hatch green chile flavor, the best of three.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 