rrections that appeared in print on Wednesday, Aug. 12, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because of an editing error, an article on Saturday about the harsher impacts that the world’s poorest communities face with the rise in global temperatures misstated the findings of a study on heat in Athens since the late 1800s. The city experienced fewer than 20 hot days in total in the decade from 1897 until 1906, not fewer than 20 hot days per year. Similarly, there were fewer than 50 hot days in total from 1987-96, not per year; and more than 120 in total from 2007-16, not per year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: Aug. 12, 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-12T03:09:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf807faf-bbc1-5439-95af-b57eb582da08', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf807faf-bbc1-5439-95af-b57eb582da08'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, August 12, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/11/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-after-virus-lockdowns-a-surge-in-homicides-haunts-major-cities.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, August 12, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We’re surrounded by murder, and it’s almost like your number is up.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: After Virus Lockdowns, A Surge in Homicides Haunts Major Cities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-12T03:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b4e357f-4c25-51b0-97a7-b5de80c7e1ee', 'word_count': 30, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b4e357f-4c25-51b0-97a7-b5de80c7e1ee'}, {'abstract': 'This has been the most painful of years in Bergamo, a proud Italian city that became synonymous with the coronavirus. As it emerges from the pandemic, one bright spot has been its title-chasing soccer team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/11/sports/soccer/atalanta-bergamo-champions-league.html', 'snippet': 'This has been the most painful of years in Bergamo, a proud Italian city that became synonymous with the coronavirus. As it emerges from the pandemic, one bright spot has been its title-chasing soccer team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERGAMO, Italy — Giorgio Gori still smiles at the memory of that night. He was sitting with his son high in the stands, watching the unimaginable unfold. The party seemed to bubble up beneath them, gathering force until it consumed them, too. “Four goals? Against Valencia? At San Siro?” he said. He phrased them as questions, as if he just needed to check what he had seen was real.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/11/sports/11soccer-bergamo02/merlin_175289961_209f8cdb-997e-4c13-a71c-1f9cfea5277e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/11/sports/11soccer-bergamo02/merlin_175289961_209f8cdb-997e-4c13-a71c-1f9cfea5277e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/11/sports/11soccer-bergamo02/merlin_175289961_209f8cdb-997e-4c13-a71c-1f9cfea5277e-jumbo.jpg', '