irus-visa-extensions.html', 'snippet': 'Many American citizens were traveling internationally when the pandemic struck. For those who have no interest in coming home in the short-term, but face expiring tourist visas, our columnist investigates the options.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am an American citizen who arrived in Mexico in January on a Forma Migratoria Múltiple, the country’s standard 180-day visitor’s permit. My daughter lives there as a temporary resident, so I’d like to stay — and, besides, I really don’t want to fly back to the States during a global pandemic. Are you aware of any concessions or extensions for travelers who, for reasons relating to Covid-19, hunkered down abroad and now realize they have overstayed their welcome? Cisco', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/travel/12tripped-up-visa/12tripped-up-visa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/17/travel/12tripped-up-visa/12tripped-up-visa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/travel/12tripped-up-visa/12tripped-up-visa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/travel/12tripped-up-visa/12tripped-up-visa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/travel/12tripped-up-visa/12tripped-up-visa-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/17/travel/12tripped-up-visa/12tripped-up-visa-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/travel/12tripped-up-visa/12tripped-up-visa-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Help! I’m Abroad and My Visa Is About to Run Out', 'kicker': 'Tripped Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Help! I’m Abroad, I Want to Stay, And My Visa Is About to Expire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel Warnings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-12T09:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Firshein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firshein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d15e9e2-a94f-5cc4-82c4-a38e1b5dc4f2', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d15e9e2-a94f-5cc4-82c4-a38e1b5dc4f2'}, {'abstract': 'Millions of Black women and their political labor have made this historic moment possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/12/opinion/kamala-harris-joe-biden-election.html', 'snippet': 'Millions of Black women and their political labor have made this historic moment possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It will be tempting for some to see Senator Kamala Harris of California’s place on the Democratic presidential ticket as a result of her race and gender, and to characterize it as an affirmative action selection. Others may see this moment as an isolated event rather than the result of the hard work of Black female candidates, political strategists and voters who have participated in the building of the Democratic Party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12price/merlin_165011979_5bb8f5a6-46ea-4a00-ae88-5b1a3bdc8556-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12price/merlin_165011979_5bb8f5a6-46ea-4a00-ae88-5b1a3bdc8556-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12price/merlin_165011979_5bb8f5a6-46ea-4a00-ae88-5b1a3bdc8556-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12price/merlin_165011979_5bb8f5a6-46ea-4a00-ae88-5b1a3bdc8556-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12price/12price-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12price/12price-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12price/12price-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Is Not Just a Victory for Kamala Harris', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Win For Black Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Kamala D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-12T09:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melanye Price', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melanye', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Price', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/65a85318-880c-54af-af6b-5c6892229737', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65a85318-880c-54af-af6b-5c6892229737'}, {'abstract': 'For service members like me, Tricare health insurance and the limited number of military medical facilities offering fertility treatments add more stress to an already emotional process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/12/magazine/infertility-military-army.html', 'snippet': 'For service members like me, Tricare health insurance and the limited number of military medical facilities offering fertility treatments add more stress to an already emotional process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The period of my life when I assumed pregnancy could be planned ended only two years ago — but it feels like a distant memory. It’s almost laughable, considering the years I spent worrying about accidental pregnancies. Once I was ready, I thought I would be in control of when and how it would happen. My husband, Mike, and I were both on active duty in the Army, with access to free medical care and paid parental leave. We had served together in two overseas duty stations and planned to start our family when we returned to the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/magazine/12atwar-infertility-4/12atwar-infertility-4-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/12/magazine/12atwar-infertility-4/12atwar-infertility-4-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/magazine/12atwar-infertility-4/12atwar-infertility-4-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/magazine/12atwar-infertility-4/12atwar-infertility-4-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1104, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/magazine/12atwar-infertility-4/12atwar-infertility-4-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/12/magazine/12atwar-infertility-4/12atwar-infertility-4-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/magazine/12atwar-infertility-4/12atwar-infertility-4-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Infertility Was Distressing. The Military Made It Even More Complicated.', 'kicker': 'at war', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'In Vitro Fertilization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reproduction (Biological)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reed, Walter, National Military Medical Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-12T09:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Chamberlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chamberlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0da8798f-9013-598e-a2c6-d1432f32d14a', 'word_count': 1950, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0da8798f-9013-598e-a2c6-d1432f32d14a'}, {'abstract': 'As an Indian-American professor of African-American history, I am experiencing Biden’s vice-presidential pick as a personal gift.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/12/opinion/kamala-harris-indian-american.html', 'snippet': 'As an Indian-American professor of African-American history, I am experiencing Biden’s vice-presidential pick as a personal gift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I arrived in the United States in 1984, an Indian graduate student wanting to study African-American history, I was an anomaly. Most of my fellow South Asians were in STEM doctoral programs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12sinha1/merlin_154692636_44d0535c-2763-4211-9e54-f2ea043bc60c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12sinha1/merlin_154692636_44d0535c-2763-4211-9e54-f2ea043bc60c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12sinha1/merlin_154692636_44d0535c-2763-4211-9e54-f2ea043bc60c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12sinha1/merlin_154692636_44d0535c-2763-4211-9e54-f2ea043bc60c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12sinha1/12sinha1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12sinha1/12sinha1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/12/opinion/12sinha1/12sinha1-thumbLarge.