 None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cf15361-1da4-5f51-acd8-e6655138df8b', 'word_count': 1292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cf15361-1da4-5f51-acd8-e6655138df8b'}, {'abstract': 'Selena Gomez hosts a cooking show from quarantine. And a new restoration of a 1960 jazz concert film is on Film Forum’s virtual cinema.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/13/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday-selena-chef-and-jazz-on-a-summers-day.html', 'snippet': 'Selena Gomez hosts a cooking show from quarantine. And a new restoration of a 1960 jazz concert film is on Film Forum’s virtual cinema.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SELENA + CHEF Stream on HBO Max. At the start of this quarantine cooking program, Selena Gomez makes a confession: “I can’t even fix eggs properly,” she says. The show pairs Gomez with famous chefs who teach her to do that and more. First up: a video call from the French chef and restaurateur Ludo Lefebvre, who instructs Gomez in the finer points of omelet making (a piece of advice: “give a little massage to the eggs with the butter”), before ramping up the difficulty, moving swiftly to soufflé. Other guest chefs during the show’s 10 episodes include Nancy Silverton, Roy Choi and Tanya Holland.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/13/arts/13tvcol-selena/13tvcol-selena-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/13/arts/13tvcol-selena/13tvcol-selena-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/13/arts/13tvcol-selena/13tvcol-selena-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr