easures of an Italian neorealist masterpiece.', 'lead_paragraph': '“People should see it — and they should care.” Those are the concluding words to one of the more passionate raves in the annals of New York Times film criticism: Bosley Crowther’s 1949 review of the Italian movie introduced to American audiences as “The Bicycle Thief.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/arts/16neorealism1/merlin_175351806_6c3c7076-d953-4383-8282-7cd574d43886-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/16/arts/16neorealism1/merlin_175351806_6c3c7076-d953-4383-8282-7cd574d43886-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/arts/16neorealism1/merlin_175351806_6c3c7076-d953-4383-8282-7cd574d43886-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 775, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/arts/16neorealism1/merlin_175351806_6c3c7076-d953-4383-8282-7cd574d43886-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1551, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/arts/16neorealism1/merlin_175351806_6c3c7076-d953-4383-8282-7cd574d43886-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/16/arts/16neorealism1/merlin_175351806_6c3c7076-d953-4383-8282-7cd574d43886-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/arts/16neorealism1/merlin_175351806_6c3c7076-d953-4383-8282-7cd574d43886-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why You Should Still Care About ‘Bicycle Thieves’', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why We Still Care About ‘Bicycle Thieves’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Sica, Vittorio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Bicycle Thief (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-13T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88cb2e92-bfb9-5a67-a409-d338b57dd6c5', 'word_count': 1422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88cb2e92-bfb9-5a67-a409-d338b57dd6c5'}, {'abstract': 'An outdated culture allowed King Juan Carlos I to become a lobbyist for Arab dictatorships and to hide his fortune for decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/13/opinion/king-juan-carlos-exile.html', 'snippet': 'An outdated culture allowed King Juan Carlos I to become a lobbyist for Arab dictatorships and to hide his fortune for decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — One of my first assignments as a reporter, in 1996, was to interview an alleged lover of the king of Spain, Juan Carlos de Borbón y Borbón. My editors at El Mundo asked me to look into whether Bárbara Rey, a Spanish film and television actress, demanded money from the state in exchange for keeping her relationship with the married king secret. In the end, I didn’t get the interview. Under pressure, Ms. Rey chose to remain silent. Thus our king’s two great weaknesses — women and money — remained the country’s worst-kept secret for another two decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15jimenez/13jimenez-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15jimenez/13jimenez-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 455}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15jimenez/13jimenez-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15jimenez/13jimenez-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1552, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15jimenez/13jimenez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15jimenez/13jimenez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15jimenez/13jimenez-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Immoral Double Life of the Former King of Spain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Families', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'El Mundo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Juan Carlos I, King of Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohammed bin Salman (1985- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-13T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jiménez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jiménez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/074be9b5-53ab-5a70-88f5-79f4730833c1', 'word_count': 1193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/074be9b5-53ab-5a70-88f5-79f4730833c1'}, {'abstract': 'How college students can stay healthy during an unpredictable fall semester.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/13/well/family/coronavirus-pandemic-college-campuses-student-health.html', 'snippet': 'How college students can stay healthy during an unpredictable fall semester.', 'lead_paragraph': 'College life was designed around community and togetherness. Now we are attempting to retrofit it for the opposite — with physical distancing, fewer people and the elimination of most in-person gatherings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/13/well/13well-college/13well-college-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/13/well/13well-college/13well-college-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/13/well/13well-college/13well-college-jumbo.jpg', '