ic education won’t be fair until school systems limit the power of white parents. But is that even possible? Chana finds two schools that are trying to do just that, and both are actually inside the I.S. 293 building. One is downstairs in the basement, where a charter school called Success Academy Cobble Hill opened about seven years ago. The other is upstairs at the newly-renamed Boerum Hill School for International Studies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Episode Four: ‘Here’s Another Fun Thing You Can Do’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boerum Hill (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cobble Hill (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Serial Productions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-13T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Podcasts', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0000da03-1036-5d08-a9ce-97d0606b09b2', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0000da03-1036-5d08-a9ce-97d0606b09b2'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Friar, a native of Northern Ireland, is chief executive of the social network Nextdoor, a sometimes unruly platform aimed at connection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/13/business/sarah-friar-nextdoor-corner-office.html', 'snippet': 'Sarah Friar, a native of Northern Ireland, is chief executive of the social network Nextdoor, a sometimes unruly platform aimed at connection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sarah Friar grew up during the Troubles. Raised in a small town in Northern Ireland, she saw neighbors turn against one another in viol