er work was discovered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/14/arts/luchita-hurtado-dead.html', 'snippet': 'For years she worked in the shadow of her artist husbands and more famous peers, painting at night when the children were asleep. Then a trove of her work was discovered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Luchita Hurtado, an artist whose paintings and drawings emphasized the interconnectedness of all living things with a visionary intensity that was almost shamanic, but whose work was recognized by the art world only late in her life, died on Thursday night at her home in Santa Monica, Calif. She was 99.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/obituaries/00Hurtado1/00Hurtado1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/15/obituaries/00Hurtado1/00Hurtado1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/obituaries/00Hurtado1/00Hurtado1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/obituaries/00Hurtado1/00Hurtado1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/obituaries/00Hurtado1/00Hurtado1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/15/obituaries/00Hurtado1/00Hurtado1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/obituaries/00Hurtado1/00Hurtado1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Luchita Hurtado, Artist Who Became a Sensation in Her 90s, Dies at 99', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Luchita Hurtado, 99, Artist Who Became a Sensation in Her 90s, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurtado, Luchita (1920-2020)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-14T13:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1b45ae6-448e-5232-b6a1-d6e1a1f43185', 'word_count': 1380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1b45ae6-448e-5232-b6a1-d6e1a1f43185'}, {'abstract': 'The safety measures in place, like glass partitions and reduced classroom sizes, eased her worries. Plus, Korean children “are even more obsessed about wearing masks than adults,” she said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/14/parenting/schools-reopening-south-korea.html', 'snippet': 'The safety measures in place, like glass partitions and reduced classroom sizes, eased her worries. Plus, Korean children “are even more obsessed about wearing masks than adults,” she said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL — I decided to send my 8-year-old daughter back to school in late May because I figured we might as well adapt to the new normal rather than run away from the coronavirus out of fear. It doesn’t look as if