'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/14/books/suffrage-famous-book-reviews.html', 'snippet': 'What did our critics think of the histories, memoirs and novels that explored the road to the 19th Amendment?', 'lead_paragraph': "On Aug. 18, 1920, the 19th amendment was ratified, marking a pivotal moment in the fight for women's rights. This centennial has provided myriad opportunities to reflect on the amendment’s legacy — from the newfound parity the vote represented to the sidelining and enduring disenfranchisement faced by women of color. Even before the amendment’s passage, debates about the women’s movement were taking place in the pages of the Book Review. Women’s history and early feminist thought were newly available to readers as writers attempted to understand the “new woman” and her goals. In these archival pieces, reviewers consider the merits of suffrage literature — and occasionally, of suffrage itself.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/obituaries/BookReviewSuffrage1/BookReviewSuffrage1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/10/obituaries/BookReviewSuffrage1/BookReviewSuffrage1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/obituaries/BookReviewSuffrage1/BookReviewSuffrage1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/obituaries/BookReviewSuffrage1/BookReviewSuffrage1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1306, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/obituaries/BookReviewSuffrage1/BookReviewSuffrage1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/10/obituaries/BookReviewSuffrage1/BookReviewSuffrage1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/10/obituaries/BookReviewSuffrage1/BookReviewSuffrage1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Battle for Women’s Suffrage Played Out in the Pages of the Book Review', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteenth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanton, Elizabeth Cady', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, H G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-14T16:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noor Qasim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qasim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf343b3c-4ef9-5c48-9afd-461f37d4f3a9', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf343b3c-4ef9-5c48-9afd-461f37d4f3a9'}, {'abstract': 'The combination of grilled lamb chops, crisp romaine lettuce hearts and creamy ranch dressing is almost a salad, but not quite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.n