lue': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-14T22:16:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lara Jakes and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jakes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40b199a1-5e4d-5c3c-9a0f-cadf37bfc6c2', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40b199a1-5e4d-5c3c-9a0f-cadf37bfc6c2'}, {'abstract': 'A thrashing in the Champions League quarterfinals showed Bayern Munich at the peak of its powers and Barcelona at the end of the line.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/14/sports/soccer/bayern-barcelona-8-2-champions-league.html', 'snippet': 'A thrashing in the Champions League quarterfinals showed Bayern Munich at the peak of its powers and Barcelona at the end of the line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lionel Messi turned his back. He had given the ball away, but he made no effort to atone for his error, no attempt to regain control. He stopped, waited a beat, and then looked to the other end of the field. It was as if he knew what was going to happen, and he did not care — or could not bear — to watch.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/sports/14onsoccer-messi-sub/merlin_175722840_8773a9f9-b154-4c38-be87-116d90a059a3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/14/spor