ph': '“I left Syria for fear of bombing — but when this happened, I wished I’d died under a bomb.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Quietly, Greece Casts Refugees Adrift in Rafts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T02:20:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/37a6c1ba-0d4d-5930-8531-a2d1a469f793', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37a6c1ba-0d4d-5930-8531-a2d1a469f793'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Saturday, Aug. 15, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/14/pageoneplus/corrections-aug-15-2020.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Saturday, Aug. 15, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Friday about the promotion of a theory by President Trump that questions Senator Kamala Harris’s eligibility to run for vice president misspelled the name of the University of California school from which Ms. Harris’s parents received doctorates. It was the University of California, Berkeley, not Berkley.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: Aug. 15, 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T02:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/78383511-30d4-5d1b-87fa-59e0fea2291c', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78383511-30d4-5d1b-87fa-59e0fea2291c'}, {'abstract': 'The president, who last week gave ByteDance 45 days to sell its stake or else face U.S. restrictions, added a 90-day deadline under a national security law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/14/business/tiktok-trump-bytedance-order.html', 'snippet': 'The president, who last week gave ByteDance 45 days to sell its stake or else face U.S. restrictions, added a 90-day deadline under a national security law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump doubled down late Friday on his previous actions against TikTok by formally giving ByteDance, the Chinese owner of the popular video-sharing app, 90 days to divest from its American assets and any data that TikTok had gathered in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/multimedia/14xp-bytedance/merlin_175409757_7264df4b-a501-461c-a9f8-259705b20cd7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/14/multimedia/14xp-bytedance/merlin_175409757_7264df4b-a501-461c-a9f8-259705b20cd7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/multimedia/14xp-bytedance/merlin_175409757_7264df4b-a501-461c-a9f8-259705b20cd7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/multimedia/14xp-bytedance/merlin_175409757_7264df4b-a501-461c-a9f8-259705b20cd7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/multimedia/14xp-bytedance/merlin_175409757_7264df4b-a501-461c-a9f8-259705b20cd7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/14/multimedia/14xp-bytedance/merlin_175409757_7264df4b-a501-461c-a9f8-259705b20cd7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/multimedia/14xp-bytedance/merlin_175409757_7264df4b-a501-461c-a9f8-259705b20cd7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Officially Orders TikTok’s Chinese Owner to Divest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TikTok (ByteDance)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Musical.ly Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee on Foreign Investment in the United States (CFIUS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T02:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Sperling', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sperling', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5f671ed-d64c-5a01-b152-d8aae208a071', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5f671ed-d64c-5a01-b152-d8aae208a071'}, {'abstract': 'Catch this engaging political documentary, and a series about dating in pre-pandemic New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday-boys-state-and-platonic.html', 'snippet': 'Catch this engaging political documentary, and a series about dating in pre-pandemic New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOYS STATE (2020) Stream on Apple TV+. Every year, hundreds of high-school-aged boys in Texas head to Austin for a weeklong mock government exercise known as Boys State. In 2018, the married filmmakers Jesse Moss and Amanda McBaine embedded in the fray, following four of the participants as their parties drafted platforms and elected key officials, including a governor. In the process, the filmmakers capture a hopeful demonstration of democracy that also reflects the hyper-polarized tensions of politics today. In her New York Times review, Manohla Dargis wrote that “the filmmakers have made an engaging movie about some kids who — as their jokes give way to debates, stratagems and even shocks — already seem to be drafting their own more interesting sequel.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/arts/15tvcol-boysstate/15tvcol-boysstate-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/15/arts/15tvcol-boysstate/15tvcol-boysstate-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/arts/15tvcol-boysstate/15tvcol-boysstate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/arts/15tvcol-boysstate/15tvcol-boysstate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/arts/15tvcol-boysstate/15tvcol-boysstate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/15/arts/15tvcol-boysstate/15tvcol-boysstate-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/arts/15tvcol-boysstate/15tvcol-boysstate-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday: ‘Boys State’ and ‘Platonic’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Messman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Messman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9b21ca4-a37c-538f-ae84-5e05f240d19b', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9b21ca4-a37c-538f-ae84-5e05f240d19b'}, {'abstract': 'N.H.L. teams’ raucous home arena traditions have persisted, with tweaks, in the postseason hub cities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/sports/hockey/vegas-golden-knights-nhl-playoffs.html', 'snippet': 'N.H.L. teams’ raucous home arena traditions have persisted, with tweaks, in the postseason hub cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDMONTON — In any other year, they would be waging battle in the Fortress, the nickname for T-Mobile Arena, where the Vegas Golden Knights notoriously defend home ice to the tune of a 75-33-11 record over three seasons, fifth-best in the N.H.L.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/sports/15nhl-arena-2/merlin_153829017_c55db069-52eb-4e86-b2ea-8878b8b589b3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/15/sports/15nhl-arena-2/merlin_153829017_c55db069-52eb-4e86-b2ea-8878b8b589b3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/sports/15nhl-arena-2/merlin_153829017_c55db069-52eb-4e86-b2ea-8878b8b589b3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/sports/15nhl-arena-2/merlin_153829017_c55db069-52eb-4e86-b2ea-8878b8b589b3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/sports/15nhl-arena-2/15nhl-arena-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/15/sports/15nhl-arena-2/15nhl-arena-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/sports/15nhl-arena-2/15nhl-arena-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recreating Home Ice, Far From Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Blackhawks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nashville Predators', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Blues', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile Arena (Las Vegas, Nev)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vegas Golden Knights', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T07:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Schram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f187378-6aba-5a23-b270-e27b2328c21f', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f187378-6aba-5a23-b270-e27b2328c21f'}, {'abstract': 'The acclaimed novelist and story writer, who died in 2003, depicted the everyday experiences and domestic concerns of women — themes that deserve more literary recognition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/books/review/carol-shields-stone-diaries-essay.html', 'snippet': 'The acclaimed novelist and story writer, who died in 2003, depicted the everyday experiences and domestic concerns of women — themes that deserve more literary recognition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Carol Shields died of breast cancer in 2003, her obituary in The New York Times remembered her as a novelist whose work highlighted the “profundity of the mundane,” while The Guardian mentioned her “commitment to commemorating otherwise ordinary lives.” Shields specialized in fiction devoted to women characters and their experience; nearly two decades later, the province of “ordinary” women in fiction still needs defending. Earlier this year, a generously endowed new literary prize for women writers was announced in Shields’s name — a choice made in part, one of the award’s founders explained, to underscore the value of domestic concerns in literature, which too often have been considered unworthy of serious fiction.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/books/review/23Huffman1/merlin_10509063_2728fed8-712d-48d9-b0de-d8f21d144440-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/23/books/review/23Huffman1/merlin_10509063_2728fed8-712d-48d9-b0de-d8f21d144440-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/books/review/23Huffman1/merlin_10509063_2728fed8-712d-48d9-b0de-d8f21d144440-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/books/review/23Huffman1/merlin_10509063_2728fed8-712d-48d9-b0de-d8f21d144440-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/books/review/23Huffman1/23Huffman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/23/books/review/23Huffman1/23Huffman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/books/review/23Huffman1/23Huffman1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Radical Ordinariness of Carol Shields’s Literary World', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chronicler of the Mundane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shields, Carol', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Stone Diaries (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naomi Huffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ea91c81-8a8d-539f-bd42-d82da420e7b8', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ea91c81-8a8d-539f-bd42-d82da420e7b8'}, {'abstract': 'Lessing’s 1962 novel is far from a manifesto. But in its embrace of chaos and split identities, it captures the mood of both its time and ours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/books/review/doris-lessing-golden-notebook.html', 'snippet': 'Lessing’s 1962 novel is far from a manifesto. But in its embrace of chaos and split identities, it captures the mood of both its time and ours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Doris Lessing, the British-Zimbabwean novelist who died in 2013, sat down to write “The Golden Notebook” in the 1950s, she was responding to a feeling of defeat in leftist circles, one similar to the whiplash experienced by liberals after the election of President Trump. The marquee intellectual philosophy of the young 20th century — communism — was sagging from the revelation that “Father Stalin” had overseen the death of millions; communist stalwarts in the West, like Lessing, felt they’d had the carpet pulled out from under them. They became intellectually homeless. Meanwhile, Senator Joseph McCarthy was raving like a proto-Trump at left-leaning Americans. What had this generation’s progressive causes amounted to?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/books/review/MahajanDigital/merlin_75868288_f2828a9d-42ec-45a2-a3b6-379f95fe87dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/07/books/review/MahajanDigital/merlin_75868288_f2828a9d-42ec-45a2-a3b6-379f95fe87dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/books/review/MahajanDigital/merlin_75868288_f2828a9d-42ec-45a2-a3b6-379f95fe87dc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/books/review/MahajanDigital/merlin_75868288_f2828a9d-42ec-45a2-a3b6-379f95fe87dc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/07/books/review/MahajanDigital/MahajanDigital-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 't