994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/890ca9f8-e534-5eac-a056-99c49e7da553'}, {'abstract': 'For some, the senator’s being on the Democratic ticket is about more than just the vice presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/opinion/kamala-harris-vice-president-biden.html', 'snippet': 'For some, the senator’s being on the Democratic ticket is about more than just the vice presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Biden’s selection of Senator Kamala Harris to be his running mate is historic. She is the first Black woman and the first person of Indian descent to be on a major-party ticket and, should Biden win, stands that much closer to becoming the first female president in our nation’s history. It’s no surprise that many Americans are emotional about her being chosen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15opreaders-kamala1/merlin_157667073_ef860fb2-f1f3-4f18-b479-0d25abb365ce-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15opreaders-kamala1/merlin_157667073_ef860fb2-f1f3-4f18-b479-0d25abb365ce-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15opreaders-kamala1/merlin_157667073_ef860fb2-f1f3-4f18-b479-0d25abb365ce-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15opreaders-kamala1/merlin_157667073_ef860fb2-f1f3-4f18-b479-0d25abb365ce-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15opreaders-kamala1/15opreaders-kamala1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15opreaders-kamala1/15opreaders-kamala1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/15/opinion/15opreaders-kamala1/15opreaders-kamala1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Kamala Harris’s Nomination Is Everything to Me’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Kamala D', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian-Americans', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel L. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/82da099e-714e-5adc-aa88-ef53dfd23446', 'word_count': 1364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82da099e-714e-5adc-aa88-ef53dfd23446'}, {'abstract': 'He’s not out on the campaign trail now, but when he was a young man in a hurry, he told us who he was.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/opinion/joe-biden-2020-1988-what-it-takes.html', 'snippet': 'He’s not out on the campaign trail now, but when he was a young man in a hurry, he told us who he was.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a reason that a certain kind of journalist makes a quadrennial habit of reading “What It Takes,” Richard Ben Cramer’s gonzo classic about the 1988 presidential primary. It’s catnip to prose snobs. It’s a New Journalism masterpiece, freckled with ellipses, popping with sound effects. And it shows, better than perhaps any campaign book in the last half-century, what metabolically and psychologically distinguishes those who seek the presidency from those who consider eight nonspectacular hours at their day jobs triumph enough.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/opinion/16senior1/merlin_166896114_a8e9b568-5f63-4268-9852-21da885b9348-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/16/opinion/16senior1/merlin_166896114_a8e9b568-5f63-4268-9852-21da885b9348-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/opinion/16senior1/merlin_166896114_a8e9b568-5f63-4268-9852-21da885b9348-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/opinion/16senior1/merlin_166896114_a8e9b568-5f63-4268-9852-21da885b9348-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/opinion/16senior1/16senior1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/16/opinion/16senior1/16senior1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/opinion/16senior1/16senior1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet Young Joe Biden, the ‘Wild Stallion’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Learning to Love Joe Biden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 1988', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'What It Takes: The Way to the White House (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cramer, Richard Ben', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T15:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Senior', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Senior', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1b895ce-dea2-5b24-9abb-52f2d8740ff0', 'word_count': 2312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1b895ce-dea2-5b24-9abb-52f2d8740ff0'}, {'abstract': 'Her parents’ arrival to Berkeley as young graduate students was the beginning of a historic wave of immigration from outside Europe that would change the United States in ways its leaders never imagined.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/us/second-generation-immigrant-kamala-harris.html', 'snippet': 'Her parents’ arrival to Berkeley as young graduate students was the beginning of a historic wave of immigration from outside Europe that would change the United States in ways its leaders never imagined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Kamala Harris’s mother left India for California in 1958, the percentage of Americans who were immigrants was at its lowest point in over a century.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/us/00HARRIS-SECONDGEN/merlin_175638150_0b3b2297-c960-4223-8495-3155842bf242-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/14/us/00HARRIS-SECONDGEN/merlin_175638150_0b3b2297-c960-4223-8495-3155842bf242-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/us/00HARRIS-SECONDGEN/merlin_175638150_0b3b2297-c960-4223-8495-3155842bf242-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/us/00HARRIS-SECONDGEN/merlin_175638150_0b3b2297-c960-4223-8495-3155842bf242-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/14/us/00HARRIS-SECONDGEN/00HARR