ype_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/171a7812-f5c2-571b-8e66-a229818b9da8', 'word_count': 1809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/171a7812-f5c2-571b-8e66-a229818b9da8'}, {'abstract': 'Francis Heaney’s the summer blockbuster this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/crosswords/daily-puzzle-2020-08-16.html', 'snippet': 'Francis Heaney’s the summer blockbuster this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY PUZZLE — The days are getting shorter and I was beginning to worry that we wouldn’t get a Sunday puzzle with a movie theme. This is a weird year for film buffs! I know that streaming services were affecting attendance long before 2020, but there were still plenty of movie theaters that employed popcorn poppers, projectionists and ushers, and I have fond memories of going to a movie during a New York summer like this one just to freeze myself for a couple of hours and recalibrate my feelings toward torrid heat. I worry now about those places and the people who made them run. On the other hand, I know that many of us have probably knocked rafts of movies off our watch lists, and there are new summer movies that went straight to the small screen, so cinematic life goes on, even if it’s limping at the moment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/crosswords/16wordplay-ravi/16wordplay-ravi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/16/crosswords/16wordplay-ravi/16wordplay-ravi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/crosswords/16wordplay-ravi/16wordplay-ravi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty