h counterprotests in a town where some would rather bridge racial divides than widen them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STONE MOUNTAIN, Ga. —\xa0A small city in the Atlanta suburbs and the big, contentious Confederate monument that shares its name seemed headed for trouble on Saturday. Far-right activists and white supremacist militia groups planned to gather at Stone Mountain to symbolically “defend” the monument, and antiracist and far-left counterprotesters planned to confront them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barred From a Confederate Shrine, Protesters Scuffle in Georgia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protesters in Georgia Face Off in Shadow  Of Confederate Shrine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'STONE MOUNTAIN (GA)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Confederate States of America', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-15T21:31:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Keenan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keenan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2cb5cf3-0a4b-5054-9e34-8108e9a043d9', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2cb5cf3-0a4b-5054-9e34-8108e9a043d9'}, {'abstract': 'Our game lets you follow the 19th Amendment’s journey from passage in the Senate to ratification by 36 states.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/15/at-home/play-suffrage-game.html', 'snippet': 'Our game lets you follow the 19th Amendment’s journey from passage in the Senate to ratification by 36 states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On June 4, 1919, the Susan B. Anthony Amendment came before the Senate. It was the fifth time that the proposal — first introduced in 1878, and already approved by the House of Representatives — had been put to senators; four months earlier, it had fallen short by just one vote. But on this day, the federal lawmakers voted 56 to 25, to pass the law, amend the constitution and establish women’s right to vote in the United States.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/multimedia/16AH-suffragegameUPDATE/16AH-suffragegameUPDATE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/16/multimedia/16AH-suffragegameUPDATE/16AH-suffragegameUPDATE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/multimedia/16AH-suffragegameUPDATE/16AH-suffragegameUPDATE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 563, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/16/multimedia/16AH-suffragegameUPDATE/16AH-suffragegameUPDATE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1126, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None