, 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hussein Mohamed and Abdi Latif Dahir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hussein', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohamed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abdi', 'middlename': 'Latif', 'lastname': 'Dahir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e9985df-dd7f-5b1b-b7e9-c4cf530c4895', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e9985df-dd7f-5b1b-b7e9-c4cf530c4895'}, {'abstract': 'Smith’s series of seasonal novels has kept pace with the world’s news, and now she brings it to a close with the arrival of Covid-19.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/17/books/review-summer-ali-smith.html', 'snippet': 'Smith’s series of seasonal novels has kept pace with the world’s news, and now she brings it to a close with the arrival of Covid-19.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A favorite bit of advice about writing criticism is from Anthony Lane, in the introduction to his collection “Nobody’s Perfect.” It’s just five words: “Never read the publicity material.” The problem, he writes, is that the provided synopses deliver “a false impression of coherence.” My corollary to Lane’s maxim would be: “Even dust jackets.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/18/books/17BOOKALISMITH1/17BOOKALISMITH1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 857, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/18/books/17BOOKALISMITH1/17BOOKALISMITH1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 857}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/18/books/17BOOKALISMITH1/17BOOKALISMITH1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 718, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/18/books/17BOOKALISMITH1/17BOOKALISMITH1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1435, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/18/books/17BOOKALISMITH1/17BOOKALISMITH1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/18/books/17BOOKALISMITH1/17BOOKALISMITH1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/18/books/17BOOKALISMITH1/17BOOKALISMITH1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ali Smith’s ‘Summer’ Ends a Funny, Political, Very Up-to-Date Quartet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Boon Companion  For These Days, Part 4', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Ali', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Summer: A Novel (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-17T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/059de4b1-0b6b-5d12-ba9d-17e9ab16b09b', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/059de4b1-0b6b-5d12-ba9d-17e9ab16b09b'}, {'abstract': 'Family members play an important role in the care we provide. I miss them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/17/opinion/coronavirus-hopsitals-visitors.html', 'snippet': 'Family members play an important role in the care we provide. I miss them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One morning in early March, during what would be our last week of normalcy, my team gathered outside our patient’s room on morning rounds. The beleaguered overnight intern began to present the details of the case. Then stopped. We needed to wait. The patient’s wife was on the way — and we couldn’t start without her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/opinion/17Lamas1/merlin_172323888_b5a5081c-48ca-4cc5-918d-ef1fb18c5913-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/17/opinion/17Lamas1/merlin_172323888_b5a5081c-48ca-4cc5-918d-ef1fb18c5913-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/opinion/17Lamas1/merlin_172323888_b5a5081c-48ca-4cc5-918d-ef1fb18c5913-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/opinion/17Lamas1/merlin_172323888_b5a5081c-48ca-4cc5-918d-ef1fb18c5913-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1321, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/opinion/17Lamas1/17Lamas1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/17/opinion/17Lamas1/17Lamas1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/opinion/17Lamas1/17Lamas1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Families Are Central to Critical Care. But the Waiting Room Is Empty.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-17T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniela J. Lamas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniela', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lamas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d269356f-33db-522f-957e-ec4f01026f8b', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d269356f-33db-522f-957e-ec4f01026f8b'}, {'abstract': 'Spending more time on screens, staying up late and sleeping late may require some adjustments for the start of the school year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/17/well/family/children-sleep-pandemic.html', 'snippet': 'Spending more time on screens, staying up late and sleeping late may require some adjustments for the start of the school year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So how are you sleeping these days? Some children — and adolescents — may actually be getting more sleep, or better sleep, while others are struggling with disrupted routines, anxiety and electronics, sometimes all at the same time. And even for those who have settled into new schedules that leave them reasonably well rested, back-to-school season may mean a possibly problematic reset.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/well/17klass-sleep/17klass-sleep-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/17/well/17klass-sleep/17klass-sleep-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/well/17klass-sleep/17klass-sleep-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/well/17klass-sleep/17klass-sleep-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/well/17klass-sleep/17klass-sleep-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/17/well/17klass-sleep/17klass-sleep-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/well/17klass-sleep/17klass-sleep-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Children’s Sleep Habits Have Changed in the Pandemic', 'kicker': 'The Checkup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject