07d74-9ea0-54ac-9edb-534dcdb4c35d'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists still have to validate the reading of 130 degrees Fahrenheit on Sunday, the equivalent of 54 degrees Celsius.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/17/climate/death-valley-hottest-temperature-on-earth.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists still have to validate the reading of 130 degrees Fahrenheit on Sunday, the equivalent of 54 degrees Celsius.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the popular imagination, Death Valley in Southern California is the hottest place on earth. At 3:41 p.m. on Sunday, it lived up to that reputation when the temperature at the aptly named Furnace Creek reached 130 degrees Fahrenheit, according to the NOAA Weather Prediction center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/multimedia/17xp-deathvalley/merlin_175821324_43bd1446-d7e5-414d-ae3b-c09aca06ee91-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/17/multimedia/17xp-deathvalley/merlin_175821324_43bd1446-d7e5-414d-ae3b-c09aca06ee91-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/multimedia/17xp-deathvalley/merlin_175821324_43bd1446-d7e5-414d-ae3b-c09aca06ee91-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/multimedia/17xp-deathvalley/merlin_175821324_43bd1446-d7e5-414d-ae3b-c09aca06ee91-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/17/multimedia/17xp-deathvalley/17xp-deathvalley-thumbS