': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-18T01:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Walker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daa64928-116f-59b9-bb83-a18c9492668c', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daa64928-116f-59b9-bb83-a18c9492668c'}, {'abstract': 'Pressoir.wine lets aficionados take part in virtual tastings and exclusive wine trips.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/17/dining/pressoir-wine.html', 'snippet': 'Pressoir.wine lets aficionados take part in virtual tastings and exclusive wine trips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pressoir.wine, an organization that holds wine events, is an extension of two wine extravaganzas — La Paulée, a series of annual celebrations, and La Fête de Champagne for Champagne tastings and dinners — founded by the sommelier Daniel Johnnes. Pressoir puts on wine trips, tastings and other events, and, with Covid-19, online Zoom wine classes with guest experts. At the end of the month, Kevin Zraly, a sommelier and teacher since 1978, will discuss the early years of his career. In advance of the talk, participants will have an opportunity to buy a bottle of Domaine Yvon Clerget Volnay Premier Cru Les Santenots 2017 he will discuss from Morrell, a wine shop.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerwine01/merlin_175578717_ca09bcf5-4a01-4ff8-85af-913221ab4838-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerwine01/merlin_175578717_ca09bcf5-4a01-4ff8-85af-913221ab4838-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerwine01/merlin_175578717_ca09bcf5-4a01-4ff8-85af-913221ab4838-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerwine01/merlin_175578717_ca09bcf5-4a01-4ff8-85af-913221ab4838-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerwine01/17burnerwine01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerwine01/17burnerwine01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerwine01/17burnerwine01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Club for Wine Lovers', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sample: Virtual Tastings For Wine Lovers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pressoir.wine (Wine Club)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnnes, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zraly, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-18T01:27:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea11220-5de7-52e6-8cfa-634353ced4f5', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea11220-5de7-52e6-8cfa-634353ced4f5'}, {'abstract': 'A group of restaurateurs has organized a fund-raiser after the devastating explosions in Lebanon’s capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/17/dining/disaster-relief-fund-for-beirut.html', 'snippet': 'A group of restaurateurs has organized a fund-raiser after the devastating explosions in Lebanon’s capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite their own economic worries during the pandemic, several restaurateurs are stepping up to provide aid to Beirut, Lebanon, after the devastation from the explosions two weeks ago. Philippe Massoud, a native of Beirut who is the chef and owner of Ilili in NoMad, along with his brother and the restaurant’s co-owner, Alexander Massoud, and the staff, have set up an emergency disaster relief fund for Beirut. Ilili and other Middle Eastern restaurants, including Au Za’atar and Balade in New York; Naya in Manhattan and Pennsylvania; Cedar’s Café in Melbourne, Fla.; and Paumanok Vineyards in Aquebogue, N.Y., are donating some or all the proceeds from the sale of special drinks or meals, a percentage of sales and other fund-raising methods, through early September. The fund, though gofundme.com, has been set in partnership with Social and Economic Action for Lebanon, a nonprofit organization established in 1997 to help the nation.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17BurnerFund01/17BurnerFund01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17BurnerFund01/17BurnerFund01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17BurnerFund01/17BurnerFund01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17BurnerFund01/17BurnerFund01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17BurnerFund01/17BurnerFund01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17BurnerFund01/17BurnerFund01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17BurnerFund01/17BurnerFund01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Raising Relief Funds for Beirut', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Give: Restaurateurs Raise  Relief Funds for Beirut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Au Za'atar (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GoFundMe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beirut (Lebanon)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ilili (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-18T01:33:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cfd424f-1cf1-5ff6-aab7-278bdcda14da', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cfd424f-1cf1-5ff6-aab7-278bdcda14da'}, {'abstract': 'Empirical, from two Noma alums, creates drinks that make use of uncommon ingredients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/17/dining/empirical-spirits.html', 'snippet': 'Empirical, from two Noma alums, creates drinks that make use of uncommon ingredients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lars Williams and Mark Emil Hermansen, both alumni of Noma in Copenhagen, were not about to can any old cocktail for their company, Empirical, which develops flavors and distilling techniques with ingredients like beet molasses, toasted birch and young pine cones. Its first canned drinks are labeled Can 01 (10 percent alcohol) and Can 02 (8 percent alcohol). These lightly carbonated drinks are blends of ingredients like oolong tea, gooseberries, sour cherry, black currant buds and walnut wood. In Can 01, a mixture the color of ripe chardonnay is a smooth, lightly fruity quaff, with tea and gooseberries at its base. Can 02 has a deep ruby color, is fairly tannic and delivers tart fruit from sour cherries and black currant buds.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerdrink01/17burnerdrink01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerdrink01/17burnerdrink01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 650}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerdrink01/17burnerdrink01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 946, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerdrink01/17burnerdrink01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1891, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerdrink01/17burnerdrink01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerdrink01/17burnerdrink01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerdrink01/17burnerdrink01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sophisticated Canned Cocktails From Copenhagen', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Refresh: Canned Cocktails  From Copenhagen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails and Mixed Drinks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Copenhagen (Denmark)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Empirical Spirits', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-18T01:36:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1544376f-95a8-52be-be9c-2a3baeb47149', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1544376f-95a8-52be-be9c-2a3baeb47149'}, {'abstract': 'Regal’s new line of King salmon is hot smoked over wood and comes in four flavors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/17/dining/regal-new-zealand-wood-roasted-king-salmon.html', 'snippet': 'Regal’s new line of King salmon is hot smoked over wood and comes in four flavors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regal, a brand of a New Zealand company that farm-raises king salmon, has introduced prepared fillets. The company, which also cultivates the highly regarded Ora King salmon, also from New Zealand, and has a green (best choice) rating from the Monterey Bay Aquarium Seafood Watch for its fish, calls this new line wood-roasted. It’s actually hot-smoked, very gently, so it retains exquisite succulence instead of the dry texture usually associated with hot-smoked salmon. The company also makes silky cold-smoked salmon. The 3.5-ounce fillets come beechwood roasted, plain, and also seasoned with chile and lime, or crusted with pepper and spices. A fourth variety, Double Manuka, roasted over manuka wood and seasoned with manuka honey, is extremely rich. The fillets each make a nice single serving and are excellent at room temperature. Through Sept. 30, 10 percent of sales through Amazon will be donated to José Andrés’s World Central Kitchen, which supports restaurants and people in need of food.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerfish01/17burnerfish01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 216, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerfish01/17burnerfish01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 216}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerfish01/17burnerfish01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerfish01/17burnerfish01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerfish01/17burnerfish01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerfish01/17burnerfish01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/17burnerfish01/17burnerfish01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From New Zealand, a Succulent Smoked Salmon', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Serve: Smoked Salmon From New Zealand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Zealand King Salmon Co Ltd (Regal)', 'rank