 {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Postal Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeJoy, Louis', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security Act (2020)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-18T09:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth Y. Goldway', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': 'Y.', 'lastname': 'Goldway', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc8b0a23-5bea-5a21-a194-8e2a94d2c835', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc8b0a23-5bea-5a21-a194-8e2a94d2c835'}, {'abstract': 'Dude, the actors are friends in real life and did have excellent adventures on the first two films in the series. Now they’re back onscreen together in the long-awaited follow-up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/18/movies/bill-ted-sequel-keanu-reeves-alex-winter.html', 'snippet': 'Dude, the actors are friends in real life and did have excellent adventures on the first two films in the series. Now they’re back onscreen together in the long-awaited follow-up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the chronicles of late-20th-century popular culture, you will find few friends as excellent as Bill S. Preston, Esq. and Ted “Theodore” Logan. The dopey Southern California dudes and bandmates always stood faithfully alongside each other, whether bumbling through time in their 1989 film debut, “Bill & Ted’s Excellent Adventure,” or wheedling themselves out of the afterlife in the 1991 sequel, “Bill & Ted’s Bogus Journey.” These movies helped bring a bodacious bounty of slang into the wider lexicon while providing early career boosts to their leading men, Alex Winter (Bill) and Keanu Reeves (Ted).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/arts/17bill-ted1/17bill-ted1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/19/arts/17bill-ted1/17bill-ted1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 617}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/arts/17bill-ted1/17bill-ted1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 997, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/arts/17bill-ted1/17bill-ted1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1993, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/arts/17bill-ted1/17bill-ted1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/19/arts/17bill-ted1/17bill-ted1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/arts/17bill-ted1/17bill-ted1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_n