t', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-18T16:03:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Astead W. Herndon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Astead', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Herndon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2efef548-a9fd-5d08-b150-b5ae2145f267', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2efef548-a9fd-5d08-b150-b5ae2145f267'}, {'abstract': 'Italian-Japanese fusion from an owner of Wayla, dining options at a lavish resort, and more restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/18/dining/nyc-restaurant-news.html', 'snippet': 'Italian-Japanese fusion from an owner of Wayla, dining options at a lavish resort, and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The West Village-based Murray’s Cheese has had aging caves in Long Island City, Queens, since 2012. Now, not far from the caves, it has opened a satellite, a cheese shop and restaurant. At the moment, the restaurant has tables on the sidewalk, socially distanced, and there’s waiter service for sandwiches, including a grilled cheese, a cheese board assortment and salads. For dinner, there’s a half roast chicken with puttanesca sauce and cheesy polenta, and a risotto. The chef is Clare Malfitano. Next to the restaurant is the well-stocked cheese shop, where no more than three customers are permitted at a time. Both spaces were designed by David Rockwell. Murray’s has also made some changes in Manhattan, moving its Mac + Cheese  from 250 Bleecker Street to 264 Bleecker Street (Leroy Street). ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/19/dining/18off/merlin_175819176_48335652-a12c-43e