9948e34a'}, {'abstract': 'In this follow-up to “Train to Busan,” a soldier turned survivor returns to a ruined country teeming with zombies and worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/20/movies/peninsula-review.html', 'snippet': 'In this follow-up to “Train to Busan,” a soldier turned survivor returns to a ruined country teeming with zombies and worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the pandemic first hit, many flashed on “Contagion,” the 2011 thriller about a world-engulfing plague. Months later, zombie movies — which divide the world into crudely opposing camps — can seem more apt. In “Night of the Living Dead,” the 1968 George A. Romero film that set loose the zombie hordes, a man teases his sister about her fears. “They’re coming to get you,” he jokes right before a zombie staggers up, attacking him and sending the sister into a house that becomes her bunker.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/00peninsula/00peninsula-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/00peninsula/00peninsula-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/00peninsula/00peninsula-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/00peninsula/00peninsula-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1054, 'width': 1874, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/00peninsula/00peninsula-thumbStandard