e Postal Service from costly retirement obligations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Louis DeJoy, the embattled postmaster general whose cost-cutting and operational changes have prompted widespread concern about mail-in voting, said on Friday he was “extremely, highly confident” the Postal Service could handle the largest vote-by-mail program in American history. He said it was “outrageous” for Democrats to suggest that he might intentionally slow ballot delivery to help President Trump.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/us/politics/21dc-postal1/21dc-postal1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/21/us/politics/21dc-postal1/21dc-postal1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/us/politics/21dc-postal1/21dc-postal1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/us/politics/21dc-postal1/21dc-postal1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1140, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/us/politics/21dc-postal1/21dc-postal1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/21/us/politics/21dc-postal1/21dc-postal1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/us/politics/21dc-postal1/21dc-postal1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'DeJoy Tells Senators Election Mail Will Be Delivered ‘Fully and on Time’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lawmakers Grill Post Office Chief Over Mail Voting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeJoy, Louis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Postal Service (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Postal Service and Post Offices', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Absentee Voting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-21T18:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Fandos and Emily Cochrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fandos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/072049c0-9a3a-53da-a38e-dc55d56bb926', 'word_count': 1517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/072049c0-9a3a-53da-a38e-dc55d56bb926'}, {'abstract': 'The new Disney+ film about a talented gorilla might leave you wondering about the real great ape that inspired the story. We have answers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/21/movies/the-real-gorilla-from-the-one-and-only-ivan.html', 'snippet': 'The new Disney+ film about a talented gorilla might leave you wondering about the real great ape that inspired the story. We have answers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can a gorilla ape Banksy? That’s the setup of Disney’s new animal rights flick, “The One and Only Ivan,” inspired by the true story of a silverback gorilla who spent 27 years intimidating children at a shopping mall in Tacoma, Wash. In the film, he becomes politicized over his imprisonment and expresses his outrage through art. Directed by Thea Sharrock and based on K.A. Applegate’s Newbery Award-winning book of the same title, this retelling is candy sweet compared with the real Ivan’s cameo in the 1991 documentary “The Urban Gorilla,” which turned him into a 500-pound cause célèbre. This computer-animated Ivan is able to speak for himself (in the voice of Sam Rockwell). As legal efforts in Germany, Argentina and the Balearic Islands have established precedents that could make primate personhood a future civil rights fight, what’s the film’s ratio of fiction to fact? We answer this and other questions below.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/21ivan-explainer4/21ivan-explainer4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 252, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/21ivan-explainer4/21ivan-explainer4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 252}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/21ivan-explainer4/21ivan-explainer4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/21ivan-explainer4/21ivan-explainer4-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/21ivan-explainer4/21ivan-explainer4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/21ivan-explainer4/21ivan-explainer4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/arts/21ivan-explainer4/21ivan-explainer4-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Answering the Many Questions About ‘The One and Only Ivan’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Curious About Ivan? A Few Facts About an Artist’s Tale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monkeys and Apes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharrock, Thea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The One and Only Ivan (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-21T18:44:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Nicholson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nicholson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a26d14c4-2ef5-5bac-b9db-3fc88e13dccf', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a26d14c4-2ef5-5bac-b9db-3fc88e13dccf'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of health workers have tested positive and some have died, while health facilities are overwhelmed and government officials are accused of stealing funds for medical supplies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/21/world/africa/kenya-doctors-strike-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of health workers have tested positive and some have died, while health facilities are overwhelmed and government officials are accused of stealing funds for medical supplies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — Doctors in public hospitals say they have not been paid, some for as long as six months. They’re furious that they’ve been given faulty protective gear, or none at all. Hundreds of government health workers have fallen sick with the coronavirus, and yet many say their medical insurance was cut in July, just when hospitals became overwhelmed with cases.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/world/21virus-kenya/21virus-kenya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/21/world/21virus-kenya/21virus-kenya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/world/21virus-kenya/21virus-kenya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/world/21virus-kenya/21virus-kenya-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/21/world/21virus-kenya/21virus-kenya-