s.com/2020/08/21/movies/black-criterion-collection.html', 'snippet': 'The prestigious Blu-ray/DVD archive is overwhelmingly white. We want to hear your suggestions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A report by Kyle Buchanan and Reggie Ugwu looked at the Criterion Collection, the trove of deluxe Blu-rays and DVDs of films by the most highly regarded filmmakers. Of more than 1,000 titles, only six were by African-American filmmakers, and none were by anyone born after 1957.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/arts/23Criterion-art/23Criterion-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/23/arts/23Criterion-art/23Criterion-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 344}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/arts/23Criterion-art/23Criterion-art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/arts/23Criterion-art/23Criterion-art-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1175, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/arts/23Criterion-art/23Criterion-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/23/arts/23Criterion-art/23Criterion-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/arts/23Criterion-art/23Criterion-art-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Would You Include in the Criterion Collection?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Criterion Collection', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-21T18:52:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05a9ab91-e708-5bcf-b5b7-bb40ea2a177d', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05a9ab91-e708-5bcf-b5b7-bb40ea2a177d'}, {'abstract': 'When ants are accidentally marked as dead, they find a way to rejoin the living.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/21/opinion/sunday/zombie-ants.html', 'snippet': 'When ants are accidentally marked as dead, they find a way to rejoin the living.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every corpse is an ecosystem. Each fallen bird, landed fish, beached whale, decomposing log, plucked flower is destined to change from a conglomerate of giant molecules, the most complex system in the universe known, into clouds and drifts of much smaller organic molecules. The process of decay is driven by scavengers, in nature beginning with vultures and blowflies and ending with fungi and bacteria.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/opinion/sunday/23wilson/23wilson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/23/opinion/sunday/23wilson/23wilson-a