'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Karni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f635ea27-ddf7-5be9-b705-8a59da859958', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f635ea27-ddf7-5be9-b705-8a59da859958'}, {'abstract': 'But what Republicans learn from the Trump era will make all the difference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/22/opinion/sunday/trump-republican-party.html', 'snippet': 'But what Republicans learn from the Trump era will make all the difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It must pain Donald Trump, deep down in his showman’s soul, to have had his convention taken away from him. The arguable peak of his presidency, the hubristic State of the Union that preceded the coronavirus, raised the reality-television elements of the address to new heights — reuniting a military family! Bestowing a Presidential Medal of Freedom! You can only imagine what brazen gimmicks, what WWE stagecraft, Trump would have rolled out for a convention taking place in normal times.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/opinion/23douthat-SR-print-1/21douthat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/23/opinion/23douthat-SR-print-1/21douthat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/23/opinion/23douthat-SR-print-1/21douthat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'c