ts, claiming “numerous incidents” of unwanted and inappropriate advances toward students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/23/us/elections/vague-allegations-against-alex-morse-offer-a-case-study-in-how-progressives-navigate-issues-of-sex-and-power.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 7, the student newspaper at the University of Massachusetts, Amherst reported that the state chapter of the College Democrats had disinvited Alex Morse, a congressional candidate and former guest lecturer at the university, from its future events, claiming “numerous incidents” of unwanted and inappropriate advances toward students.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vague allegations against Alex Morse offer a case study in how progressives navigate issues of sex and power.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-23T13:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Elections', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9780091-3783-57ee-94bf-86fe5e577ae4', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9780091-3783-57ee-94bf-86fe5e577ae4'}, {'abstract': 'The burst of creativity that has swept through town in recent weeks could provide a road map for other cities confronting historical racism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/23/arts/design/black-artists-portland.html', 'snippet': 'The burst of creativity that has swept through town in recent weeks could provide a road map for other cities confronting historical racism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the years, Bobby Fouther has watched the historic center of African-American life in Portland bloom, shrink and expand again. The 69-year-old artist was born into a creative family from the neighborhood of Albina, which he remembers filled with jazz music and beauty. “Black artists were thriving here in the 1950s,” he recalled. “My parents had turned our grandfather’s garage into a miniature theater, where my stepfather and his friends would perform late into the night.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/24/arts/23portland-artists1/23portland-artists1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/24/arts/23portland-artists1/23portland-artists1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 687}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/24/arts/23portland-artists1/23portland-artists1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 894, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/24/arts/23portland-artists1/23portland-artists1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1788, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/24/arts/23portland-artists1/23portland-artists1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/24/arts/23portland-artists1/23portland-artists1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/24/arts/23portland-artists1/23portland-arti