html', 'snippet': 'Wild violet corn is a new seasonal offering from Baldor Specialty Foods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ears of corn with purple kernels among the gold are new on the market from Baldor Specialty Foods, the wholesale company that has been delivering to retail customers during the pandemic. The corn, which comes already shucked in packs of four, is grown in Florida and New Jersey. It has the meaty, rich flavor and texture of mature corn. Baldor also carries baby corn, ears 3- to 6-inches long, sold in the husk. It’s not a dwarf variety, but regular sweet corn grown at Alewife Farm in Kingston, N.Y., and picked very young; even the central cob is tender. The smallest ones can be enjoyed raw in an assortment of crudités; larger ones are better sliced thin into a stir-fry or taco, or parboiled whole and served as a side dish. The season on these new varieties will extend into September.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26Burnercorn01/17Burnercorn01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26Burnercorn01/17Burnercorn01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26Burnercorn01/17Burnercorn01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26Burnercorn01/17Burnercorn01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26Burnercorn01/17Burnercorn01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26Burnercorn01/17Burnercorn01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26Burnercorn01/17Burnercorn01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Corn With a Purple Blush', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Nibble: Corn With a Purple Blush Is a New Seasonal Offering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baldor Specialty Foods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-24T19:07:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fd720c0-e02f-54ea-9be4-c98fea5a73ff', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fd720c0-e02f-54ea-9be4-c98fea5a73ff'}, {'abstract': 'Perfect for an antipasto platter, these preserved tomatoes, artichokes and zucchini also work nicely in a sandwich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/24/dining/missy-robbins-jarred-vegetables.html', 'snippet': 'Perfect for an antipasto platter, these preserved tomatoes, artichokes and zucchini also work nicely in a sandwich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though Missy Robbins is known for homemade pasta at her two Brooklyn restaurants, Lilia and Misi, she is also an expert when it comes to preparing vegetables. Jarred marinated and grilled artichokes (16 ounces, $17), slow-roasted tomatoes in olive oil (12 ounces, $18), and lemon and garlic marinated zucchini (6 ounces, $16) are superb additions to salads, antipasto platters, sandwiches and even pasta dishes. The preserves are all from MP Specialties, one of the departments in her online store, and available for pickup at locations throughout the tristate area.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-jar/26burner-jar-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-jar/26burner-jar-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-jar/26burner-jar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-jar/26burner-jar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2028, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-jar/26burner-jar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-jar/26burner-jar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-jar/26burner-jar-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jarred Vegetables From the Chef Missy Robbins', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Serve: Preserves That Add Pop To a Sandwich or a Salad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Missy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zucchini', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artichokes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MisiPasta Specialties (Brooklyn, NY, Retailer)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-24T19:13:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75549cd6-c603-58a1-b407-40f93e69ad3e', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75549cd6-c603-58a1-b407-40f93e69ad3e'}, {'abstract': 'Organic Mixology’s new chocolate and sea salt liqueur adds a sophisticated note to cocktails like the sidecar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/24/dining/om-chocolate-liqueur.html', 'snippet': 'Organic Mixology’s new chocolate and sea salt liqueur adds a sophisticated note to cocktails like the sidecar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Organic Mixology, or OM, a line of intriguing liqueurs in combinations like Meyer Lemon & Ginger, has introduced a Dark Chocolate & Sea Salt flavor. This is not your often-cloying garden-variety chocolate spirit, but one that showcases the bitterness of dark chocolate, with the salt a subtle grace note. The company suggests using it in a sidecar or espresso martini, but I successfully added a splash to an iced coffee shakerato. And I was pleased at how nicely it came through in a 3-2-1 cocktail of dark rum, chocolate liqueur and elderflower liqueur.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-sip/24burner-sip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-sip/24burner-sip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 817}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-sip/24burner-sip-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 753, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-sip/24burner-sip-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1505, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-sip/24burner-sip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-sip/24burner-sip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/dining/26burner-sip/24burner-sip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Chocolate Liqueur Is a Keeper', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline