rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hyderabad (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-25T13:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geneva Abdul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geneva', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abdul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c11e53e-d81f-5e69-bf2b-803e58616c56', 'word_count': 1206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c11e53e-d81f-5e69-bf2b-803e58616c56'}, {'abstract': 'These performers are creating a new template for the artist-as-activist, challenging their industry — and their audiences — to reconsider what inclusion really means.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/25/t-magazine/actors-disability-theater-film-tv.html', 'snippet': 'These performers are creating a new template for the artist-as-activist, challenging their industry — and their audiences — to reconsider what inclusion really means.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RYAN O’CONNELL would like you to know that he is tired and pissed off and horny. He is tired of waiting for what he calls “our ‘Transparent’ moment” (some of his fellow actors call it, instead, “our ‘Pose’ moment”), by which he means a single piece of breakthrough pop culture that makes people aware of a heretofore ignored and stereotyped minority, a prizewinning, noisemaking event that kicks open the door to mainstream omnipresence and ultimately to normalization. He is pissed off that it hasn’t happened yet. “I think about this a lot,” he says. “Why, in this woke-ass culture that we live in, where so much attention is given to marginalized populations, do people with disabilities still largely go ignored?” The actor, who has cerebral palsy, is also, he says, “horny for representation that comes from actual disabled people, because we live in a dark hellscape of a capitalist country. Real power can only be accrued through opportunities, and you need to be given the keys to tell your own story.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO/30tmag-disabled-actors-slide-29TO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Actors With Disabilities Redefining Representation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deaf West Theater Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stroker, Ali (1987- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferris, Madison', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gottsagen, Zack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozgala, Gregg', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connell, Ryan (Actor)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shinn, Christopher', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wailes, Alexandria', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-25T13:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9069205d-f220-5be6-93f4-7f20a3ab60b1', 'word_count': 5005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9069205d-f220-5be6-93f4-7f20a3ab6