tps://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/26/health/covid-19-superspreaders-boston.html', 'snippet': 'A February meeting of biotech executives became a coronavirus “superspreading” event with a transmission chain across the globe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Feb. 26, 175 executives at the biotech company Biogen gathered at a Boston hotel for the first night of a conference. At the time, the coronavirus seemed a faraway problem, limited mostly to China.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/science/26VIRUS-BOSTON1/merlin_176194980_6fed9726-17e9-4770-8151-2987ccbac385-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/26/science/26VIRUS-BOSTON1/merlin_176194980_6fed9726-17e9-4770-8151-2987ccbac385-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/science/26VIRUS-BOSTON1/merlin_176194980_6fed9726-17e9-4770-8151-2987ccbac385-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/science/26VIRUS-BOSTON1/merlin_176194980_6fed9726-17e9-4770-8151-2987ccbac385-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/science/26VIRUS-BOSTON1/26VIRUS-BOSTON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/26/science/26VIRUS-BOSTON1/26VIRUS-BOSTON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/science/26VIRUS-BOSTON1/26VIRUS-BOSTON1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Meeting in Boston Seeded Tens of Thousands of Infections, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'Matter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-healthcare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-26T13:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Zimmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zimmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8b981e6-4413-5640-9909-acb60fff8ed2', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8b981e6-4413-5640-9909-acb60fff8ed2'}, {'abstract': 'The statement-making collar also features diamonds and a standout purplish-pink kunzite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/26/t-magazine/cartier-necklace-surnaturel.html', 'snippet': 'The statement-making collar also features diamonds and a standout purplish-pink kunzite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The panther has been Cartier’s leitmotif for more than a century. The first time the Paris-based jewelry company, founded in 1847, alluded to the graceful jungle cat was in 1914, when the house created a women’s platinum wristwatch with a case that resembled an abstracted version of the elegant animal’s spots, in onyx and diamonds. In the decades that followed, the house, led by creative director Jeanne Toussaint, interpreted the panther in increasingly figurative ways, culminating in the three-dimensional brooches and bracelet made for the Duchess of Windsor in the late 1940s and ’50s, in which the animal’s emerald or diamond eyes seemed to glow.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '71', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-thing-copy/30tmag-thing-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-thing-copy/30tmag-thing-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-thing-copy/30tmag-thing-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-thing-copy/30tmag-thing-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-thing-copy/30tmag-thing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-thing-copy/30tmag-thing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-thing-copy/30tmag-thing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 15