 have lost power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/us/hurricane-laura-update.html', 'snippet': 'After landfall overnight with 150 m.p.h. winds, Laura ripped northward. Officials confirmed at least six deaths tied to the storm, and hundreds of thousands of people have lost power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hurricane Laura, which began the day rolling ashore as one of the strongest storms ever to hit Louisiana, plowed trough the state from south to north, gradually weakening to become a tropical storm but wreaking destruction all along its path and killing at least six people before the afternoon was through.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hurricane Laura Kills at Least 6 People in Louisiana', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Laura (2020)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf Coast (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Failures and Blackouts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-27T06:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1207a023-e98b-5dfd-a379-fb1461e5772a', 'word_count': 4485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1207a023-e98b-5dfd-a379-fb1461e5772a'}, {'abstract': 'The pseudo-medieval morality tale “Jedermann” inaugurated the first Salzburg Festival with an outdoor performance in 1920. The world premiere of “Everywoman” expands the concept beyond Salzburg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/theater/jedermann-everywoman-salzburg.html', 'snippet': 'T