}, {'abstract': 'Two of our reporters break down the key moments from the third night of the Republican National Convention.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/us/politics/rnc-convention.html', 'snippet': 'Two of our reporters break down the key moments from the third night of the Republican National Convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Nagourney: The third night of the Republican National Convention took place against a backdrop of staggering tumult in the country: the demonstrations and shootings in Kenosha, Wis., the devastating hurricane approaching the Gulf Coast. The big question was whether the speakers would at last mention these issues. The answer, particularly with Vice President Mike Pence’s speech, was yes, they were mentioned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Major Themes From Night 3 of the R.N.C.: Watch the Highlights', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-27T09:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shane Goldmacher and Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldmacher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/131f38dc-719a-5710-ae85-56080795910c', 'word_count': 1628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/131f38dc-719a-5710-ae85-56080795910c'}, {'abstract': 'Decades after the war ended, scars left by the Japanese occupation persist for millions of Koreans and Korean-Americans, including the author Alexander Chee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/magazine/korea-japanese-occupation-surrender-ww2.html', 'snippet': 'Decades after the war ended, scars left by the Japanese occupation persist for millions of Koreans and Korean-Americans, including the author Alexander Chee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest article from “Beyond the World War II We Know,” a series by The Times that documents lesser-known stories from World War II, the author Alexander Chee looks back at the dark legacy of the Japanese occupation of Korea — and a once-unknown personal connection to it.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/09/06/multimedia/27ww2-korea-02/merlin_176126850_ed49f72d-d32e-4e82-a406-42b5c387e87c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/09/06/multimedia/27ww2-korea-02/merlin_176126850_ed49f72d-d32e-4e82-a406-42b5c387e87c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/09/06/multimedia/27ww2-korea-02/merlin_176126850_ed49f72d-d32e-4e82-a406-42b5c387e87c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/09/06/multimedia/27ww2-korea-02/merlin_176126850_ed49f72d-d32e-4e82-a406-42b5c387e87c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1661, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/09/06/multimedia/27ww2-korea-02/27ww2-korea-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/09/06/multimedia/27ww2-korea-02/27ww2-korea-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/09/06/multimedia/27ww2-korea-02/27ww2-korea-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Family’s Shrouded History Is Also a National One for Korea', 'kicker': 'Beyond the World War II We Know', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Would a Korean  Grandfather Dream  In Japanese? The Scars Of an Occupation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-27T09:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SpecialSections', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Chee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7b36480-76d3-5994-90b8-50fb61dfd8eb', 'word_count': 1715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7b36480-76d3-5994-90b8-50fb61dfd8eb'}, {'abstract': 'The young people leading the huge volunteer effort after the recent blast are bringing hope, but have lost it themselves. “I want to at least have Beirut on its feet before I go,” one said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/wo