 between race, social class and a quality education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The podcast “Nice White Parents” largely focuses on the story of one Brooklyn middle school that opened in 1968 — and how white parents have influenced the trajectory of this school over and over, even when their children didn’t attend it. But the issues the podcast raises via this one case study make it a meaningful opportunity to explore the complicated realities of race, privilege and power across all American schools.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/20/learning/NWPDiscussionArt-LN/NWPDiscussionArt-LN-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/20/learning/NWPDiscussionArt-LN/NWPDiscussionArt-LN-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/20/learning/NWPDiscussionArt-LN/NWPDiscussionArt-LN-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/20/learning/NWPDiscussionArt-LN/NWPDiscussionArt-LN-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/20/learning/NWPDiscussionArt-LN/NWPDiscussionArt-LN-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/20/learning/NWPDiscussionArt-LN/NWPDiscussionArt-LN-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/20/learning/NWPDiscussionArt-LN/NWPDiscussionArt-LN-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Nice White Parents’ Discussion Guide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-27T13:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'subsection_name': 'Lesson Plans', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Daniels and Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Daniels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed98c3c1-2525-5da1-9e26-0fcf02b0b344', 'word_count': 4500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed98c3c1-2525-5da1-9e26-0fcf02b0b344'}, {'abstract': 'From ancient times through today, the same blooms used to harm have also proved healing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/t-magazine/poisonous-flowers-healing-plants.html', 'snippet': 'From ancient times through today, the same blooms used to harm have also proved healing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FLOWERS POINT straight down, a chandelier’s worth, turned ostentatiously away from the sun. They are Brugmansia by genus and angel’s trumpet in parlance, with elongated buds that open into blaring mouths. In South America, the tree that bears them is called el borrachero, or “the drunk-maker,” in part because of the blooms’ dizzying night perfume of fermented lemons, said to induce crazed dreams. And more: Parts of the plant, when crushed, yield scopolamine, a.k.a. burundanga, a.k.a. devil’s breath — a psychoactive alkaloid deployed by criminals, via a spiked drink or a puff in the face, to disable free will. It is said to transform victims into dutiful servants who revive hours later, bereft of all their belongings and any memory of what they’ve done.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '102', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/t-magazine/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS/30tmag-poison-flowers-slide-SRXS-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dual History of Poisonous Flowers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Killing Kind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Emily (Florist)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-27T14:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3133fc3e-8a65-5e10-9c5a-49bc9cc53407', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3133fc3e-8a65-5e10-9c5a-49bc9cc53407'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon’s irreverent take on the superhero genre is defined by depravity and violence, which makes it suited to a time when “authoritarianism and celebrity are combined,” its creator said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/arts/television/the-boys-amazon.html', 'snippet': 'Amazon’s irreverent take on the superhero genre is defined by depravity and violence, which makes it suited to a time when “authoritarianism and celebrity are combined,” its creator said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the penultimate episode of the new season of “The Boys,” Amazon’s superhero action series, and it’s time for a costumed champion named Starlight to give one of those rousing speeches that inspires listeners to ignore insurmountable odds and get motivated for the journey ahead.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/arts/30the-boys2/30the-boys2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/30/arts/30the-boys2/30the-boys2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/arts/30the-boys2/30the-boys2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/arts/30the-boys2/30the-boys2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/arts/30the-boys2/30the-boys2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/30/arts/30the-boys2/30the-boys2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/arts/30the-boys2/30the-boys2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Boys’ Is Back, More Relevant Than Ever', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hero Here Is Hard to Find', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Boys (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kripke, Eric (1974- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-27T14:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/140711ca-c053-51c6-a764-6529d7687b62', 'word_count': 1735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/140711ca-c053-51c6-a764-6529d7687b62'}, {'abstract': 'In 1996, the activist artist found inspiration at two of his favorite museums. The discussion that followed, with a Times critic, revealed a man of his generation, whose art is as timely as ever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/arts/design/jacob-lawrence-metropolitan-museum.html', 'snippet': 'In 1996, the activist artist found inspiration at two of his favorite museums. The discussion that followed, with a Times critic, revealed a man of his generation, whose art is as timely as ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shuttered since March by the coronavirus pandemic, the Museum of Modern Art and the Metropolitan Museum of Art are reopening with limited visitorship, various admonitions about masks and social distancing, and several new exhibitions, among them “Jacob Lawrence: The American Struggle.” That show, at the Met, reunites the panels of a lesser-known series that the storied modernist painted during the mid-1950s, exploring themes from the American Revolution to the Westward expansion. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/28/arts/27kimmelman-lawrence1/27kimmelman-lawrence1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/28/arts/27kimmelman-lawrence1/27kimmelman-lawrence1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/28/arts/27kimmelman-lawrence1/27kimmelman-lawrence1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/28/arts/27kimmelman-lawrence1/27kimmelman-lawrence1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 1496, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/28/arts/27kimmelman-lawrence1/27kimmelman-lawrence1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/28/arts/27kimmelman-lawrence1/27kimmelman-lawrence1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/28/arts/27kimmelman-lawrence1/27kimmelman-lawrence1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In His Own Words: Jacob Lawrence at the Met and MoMA', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jacob Lawrence at the Met and MoMA', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Jacob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knight, Gwendolyn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-27T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kimmelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kimmelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4136300d-8797-5008-890d-e8ca94cebf4a', 'word_count': 1761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4136300d-8797-5008-890d-e8ca94cebf4a'}, {'abstract': 'On the third day of the convention, Vice President Mike Pence and other Republicans portrayed Democrats as tolerant of violence and riots. And they continued to try to soften President Trump’s image.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/us/elections/republicans-have-intensified-their-unrest-focused-message-with-kenosha-as-a-backdrop.html', 'snippet': 'On the third day of the convention, Vice President Mike Pence and other Republicans portrayed Democrats as tolerant of violence and riots. And they continued to try to soften President Trump’s image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans used the third night of their convention on Wednesday to amplify warnings of violence and lawlessness under Democratic leadership, trying to capitalize on the worsening unrest in Wisconsin to reclaim moderate voters who might be reluctant to hand President Trump a second term.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans have intensified their unrest-focused message, with Kenosha as a backdrop.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-08-27T14:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Elections', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin and Alexander Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fc4b4f5-3fc2-5283-b69b-d464c7ba18bf', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fc4b4f5-3fc2-5283-b69b-d464c7ba18bf'}, {'abstract': 'On one of the most consequential nights in recent sports history — when a player-led boycott forced the N.B.A. to postpone playoff games — the Republican National Convention offered pro-Trump testimonials from a retired Notre Dame coach and a former N.F.L. player facing insider-trading charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/27/us/elections/as-young-black-athletes-call-for-a-racial-awakening-some-nfl-retirees-declare-fealty-to-trump.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'On one of the most consequential nights in recent sports history — when a player-led boycott forced the N.B.A. to postpone playoff games — the Republican National Convention offered pro-Trump testimonials from a retired Notre Dame coach and a former N.F.L. player facing insider-trading charges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/us/politics/26elections-briefing-thrush-26-22-33/merlin_176215461_ce81bacd-9373-4c27-836d-06032f03581b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/26/us/politics/26elections-briefing-thrush-26-22-33/merlin_176215461_ce81bacd-9373-4c27-836d-06032f03581b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/26/us/politics/26elections-briefing-thrush-26-22