://article/87cbbf79-d275-5eaa-9a98-8929f21af9c4'}, {'abstract': 'Brains are talking to computers, and computers to brains. Are our daydreams safe?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/28/opinion/sunday/brain-machine-artificial-intelligence.html', 'snippet': 'Brains are talking to computers, and computers to brains. Are our daydreams safe?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jack Gallant never set out to create a mind-reading machine. His focus was more prosaic. A computational neuroscientist at the University of California, Berkeley, Dr. Gallant worked for years to improve our understanding of how brains encode information — what regions become active, for example, when a person sees a plane or an apple or a dog — and how that activity represents the object being viewed.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Brain Implants That Could Change Humanity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mind Readers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voice Recognition Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paralysis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sensors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Implants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Touch (Sense)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gallant, Jack L', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yuste, Rafael', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirsch, Robert F', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chang, Edward F', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halpern, Casey H', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Addiction (Psychology)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-28T09:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Moises Velasquez-Manoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Moises', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Velasquez-Manoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c69399f0-8e69-54b7-84ed-19762ac90d80', 'word_count': 4881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c69399f0-8e69-54b7-84ed-19762ac90d80'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hallberg, soon to lead the Australian Ballet, was photographed in Moscow before the pandemic halted his final days as a dancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/28/arts/dance/david-hallberg-bolshoi.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hallberg, soon to lead the Australian Ballet, was photographed in Moscow before the pandemic halted his final days as a dancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Hallberg is not on a plane. He is not dashing between Moscow and Milan, London and Sydney, readjusting to time zones, settling into rented apartments, reconnecting with favorite partners and old friends. Mr. Hallberg, 38, who made ballet history in 2011 by becoming the first American to join the Bolshoi Ballet as a principal, is not rehearsing and performing in “Eugene Onegin,” “Giselle,” “The Winter’s Tale” or “Nureyev”— some of the ballets he was supposed to dance this year, with the Bolshoi Ballet, American Ballet Theater, the Royal Ballet and La Scala Ballet.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag