'lead_paragraph': 'Heather Boushey, who is unofficially one of the top economic advisers to Joseph R. Biden Jr., does not play to type. When the progressive economist and I arranged to meet last December in a Midtown Manhattan coffee shop, I was expecting someone buttoned up, and I couldn’t find her in the room. Then she texted and waved from just a few feet away. She was wearing a Stephen Malkmus and the Jicks T-shirt — a niche band featuring the lead singer of the beloved 1990s indie group Pavement.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/25/business/00BOUSHEY-02/00BOUSHEY-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/25/business/00BOUSHEY-02/00BOUSHEY-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/25/business/00BOUSHEY-02/00BOUSHEY-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/25/business/00BOUSHEY-02/00BOUSHEY-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/25/business/00BOUSHEY-02/00BOUSHEY-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/25/business/00BOUSHEY-02/00BOUSHEY-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/25/business/00BOUSHEY-02/00BOUSHEY-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Gen-X Adviser to Biden Argues Equality Is Good for Growth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Equality? That’s What’s Good for Growth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boushey, Heather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Center for Equitable Growth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security Act (2020)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Finding Time: The Economics of Work-Life Conflict (Book)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Unbound: How Inequality Constricts Our Economy and What We Can Do About It (Book)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-28T15:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katy Lederer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lederer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fb2724b-75ea-59e8-9143-9deba7f16919', 'word_count': 1592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fb2724b-75ea-59e8-9143-9deba7f16919'}, {'abstract': 'The rookie guard has been ste