rders and Memorandums', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beijing Bytedance Technology Co Ltd', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-29T18:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Mozur, Raymond Zhong and David McCabe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mozur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Raymond', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zhong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCabe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccc0d8d2-5a37-563e-bbb2-a476a5fe6522', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccc0d8d2-5a37-563e-bbb2-a476a5fe6522'}, {'abstract': 'Why are some schools pressuring student-athletes to play a game that could expose them to the coronavirus?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/29/opinion/sunday/college-football-covid.html', 'snippet': 'Why are some schools pressuring student-athletes to play a game that could expose them to the coronavirus?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than six months now, many workers deemed essential have had to strap on face masks for shifts at meatpacking plants, Walmarts, grocery stores, hardware stores and restaurants. It is a necessary sacrifice for the nation’s well-being. But at universities across the country, while scores of professors, staff and students start the academic year remotely to curb the spread