ldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a7ffd7e-55d8-5d84-aa24-e7c2745acaf6', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a7ffd7e-55d8-5d84-aa24-e7c2745acaf6'}, {'abstract': 'The elimination of in-person election security briefings to Congress could leave the public with a diminished understanding of the threats facing the election as it enters a critical phase.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/30/us/politics/2020-election-security-briefings.html', 'snippet': 'The elimination of in-person election security briefings to Congress could leave the public with a diminished understanding of the threats facing the election as it enters a critical phase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The decision by the nation’s top intelligence official to halt classified, in-person briefings to Congress about foreign interference in a presidential election that is just nine weeks away exposes the fundamental tension about who needs to know this information: just the president, or the voters whose election infrastructure, and minds, are the target of the hacking?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/us/politics/30dc-intel/merlin_172211034_1dd03939-263b-44df-9d3d-fe8a5e757616-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/30/us/politics/30dc-intel/merlin_172211034_1dd03939-263b-44df-9d3d-fe8a5e757616-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/30/us/politics/30dc-intel/merlin_172211034_1dd03939-263b-44d