as been withdrawn from the tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/31/sports/tennis/us-open-coronavirus-contact-tracing.html', 'snippet': 'These athletes did not test positive for the coronavirus themselves, but they had close contact with an infected athlete who has been withdrawn from the tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might think Kristina Mladenovic would have been nothing but delighted on Monday after winning her first match in the first Grand Slam tennis tournament since the coronavirus pandemic disrupted tennis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/31/sports/31usopen-live04/merlin_176409840_b2354725-7572-4a4f-adf0-502498eae46f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/31/sports/31usopen-live04/merlin_176409840_b2354725-7572-4a4f-adf0-502498eae46f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/31/sports/31usopen-live04/merlin_176409840_b2354725-7572-4a4f-adf0-502498eae46f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/31/sports/31usopen-live04/merlin_176409840_b2354725-7572-4a4f-adf0-502498eae46f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/31/sports/31usopen-live04/31usopen-live04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/31/sports/31usopen-live04/31usopen-live04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/31/sports/31usopen-live04/31usopen-live04-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Contact Tracing, Some U.S. Open Players Are Put on Tighter Restrictions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Bubble in a Bubble’ Is Imposed After a Top French Player Is Withdrawn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contact Tracing (Public Health)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Billie Jean King National Tennis Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paire, Benoit', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-31T21:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b64d8fa7-c1c9-501d-ad2f-fef2d0f60892', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b64d8fa7-c1c9-501d-ad2f-fef2d0f60892'}, {'abstract': 'Throughout his career, Simon Watson has brought his unique eye to crumbling castles, monastic apartments and everything in between.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/31/t-magazine/simon-watson-photographer-book-design.html', 'snippet': 'Throughout his career, Simon Watson has brought his unique eye to crumbling castles, monastic apartments and everything in between.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1530s, Cardinal Marcello Cervini, the future Pope Marcellus II, bought Castello Cervini, a medieval monastery surrounded by chestnut trees in Tuscany’s Vivo d’Orcia estate. And while Marcellus II passed away just 22 days after ascending to the papacy in 1555, his family has retained the property for four centuries and counting. By the time the photographer Simon Watson visited, in 2002, Marcellus’s descendants Daria Cervini and her siblings had turned the castle into a summer retreat, but many tokens of the family’s past remained, and a portrait of the ill-fated pope in a crimson mozzetta kept watch over all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/27/t-magazine/design/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/27/t-magazine/design/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 464}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/27/t-magazine/design/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/27/t-magazine/design/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1582, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/27/t-magazine/design/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/27/t-magazine/design/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/27/t-magazine/design/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P/simon-watson-slide-NJ1P-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Book from a Renowned Photographer of Interiors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Simon (Photographer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-08-31T21:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Conrad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Conrad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fb1130c-270c-5573-9014-2d748e5f3056', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fb1130c-270c-5573-9014-2d748e5f3056'}, {'abstract': 'The Mount Kisco, N.Y., company teamed up with the Metropolitan Museum to create a special assortment of bars as fund-raisers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/08/31/dining/metropolitan-museum-mast-brothers-chocolate.html', 'snippet': 'The Mount Kisco, N.Y., company teamed up with the Metropolitan Museum to create a special assortment of bars as fund-raisers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mast, the chocolate makers originally based in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, but now in Mount Kisco, N.Y., teamed up with the Metropolitan Museum of Art two years ago to create a special assortment of bars for the gift shop, each wrapped in paintings from the Met. Some are notably well matched, like Katsushika Hokusai’s “Under the Wave Off Kanagawa” for a bar of sea salt chocolate, and John Singer Sargent’s “Madame X” with dark chocolate. As a fund-raiser for its 150th anniversary, the collection of chocolate bars in a dozen flavors will benefit the museum. For each $9 bar, $5.50 will go to the Met; for the $100 set, $60 is donated. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/09/02/dining/02Burner-Met-Combo-a/merlin_176233467_07a9933e-088e-4e36-ab63-0aa660889f22-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/09/02/dining/02Burner-Met-Combo-a/merlin_176233467_07a9933e-088e-4e36-ab63-0aa660889f22-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/09/02/dining/02Burner-Met-Combo-a/merlin_176233467_07a9933e-088e-4e36-ab63-0aa660889f22-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/09/02/dining/02Burner-Met-Combo-a/merlin_176233467_07a9933e-088e-4e36-ab63-0aa660889f22-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, 